/* AI brain Q&A pack 26: phrases in 30 languages */
(window.AIQA = window.AIQA || []).push(
  ["how do you say good morning in spanish | good morning in spanish | spanish for good morning", "In Spanish, good morning is **buenos días** (*BWEH-nohs DEE-ahs*). In the afternoon switch to **buenas tardes**."],
  ["how do you say good night in spanish | good night in spanish | goodnight in spanish", "In Spanish, good night is **buenas noches** (*BWEH-nahs NOH-chehs*). It also works as \"good evening\"."],
  ["how do you say how are you in spanish | how are you in spanish | spanish for how are you", "In Spanish, \"how are you?\" is **¿Cómo estás?** (*KOH-moh ehs-TAHS*). To be polite with an adult, say **¿Cómo está usted?** A common reply is **Bien, gracias** (fine, thanks)."],
  ["how do you say my name is in spanish | my name is in spanish | what is your name in spanish", "In Spanish, \"my name is …\" is **Me llamo …** (*meh YAH-moh*) — just add your name. To ask someone's name: **¿Cómo te llamas?** (*KOH-moh teh YAH-mahs*)"],
  ["how do you say i love you in spanish | i love you in spanish | spanish for i love you", "In Spanish, \"I love you\" is **Te quiero** (*teh kee-EH-roh*). **Te quiero** is what people say to family and friends. **Te amo** is a deeper, more romantic love."],
  ["how do you say happy birthday in spanish | happy birthday in spanish | spanish for happy birthday", "In Spanish, \"happy birthday\" is **¡Feliz cumpleaños!** (*feh-LEES koom-pleh-AH-nyohs*)."],
  ["how do you say sorry in spanish | how do you say excuse me in spanish | sorry in spanish | excuse me in spanish", "In Spanish, \"excuse me\" is **Disculpe** (*dees-KOOL-peh*) and \"sorry\" is **Lo siento** (*loh see-EHN-toh*). For a quick \"oops, pardon\", say **perdón** (*pehr-DOHN*)."],
  ["how do you say where is the bathroom in spanish | where is the bathroom in spanish | where is the toilet in spanish", "In Spanish, \"where is the bathroom?\" is **¿Dónde está el baño?** (*DOHN-deh ehs-TAH el BAH-nyoh*)."],
  ["how do you say i don't understand in spanish | i don't understand in spanish | i dont understand in spanish", "In Spanish, \"I don't understand\" is **No entiendo** (*noh ehn-tee-EHN-doh*). To ask them to repeat: **¿Puede repetir, por favor?**"],
  ["how do you say do you speak english in spanish | do you speak english in spanish | how to ask if someone speaks english in spanish", "In Spanish, \"do you speak English?\" is **¿Habla inglés?** (*AH-blah een-GLEHS*). With a friend: **¿Hablas inglés?**"],
  ["how do you say how much is this in spanish | how much is this in spanish | how much does it cost in spanish", "In Spanish, \"how much is this?\" is **¿Cuánto cuesta?** (*KWAHN-toh KWEHS-tah*)."],
  ["how do you say nice to meet you in spanish | nice to meet you in spanish | spanish for nice to meet you", "In Spanish, \"nice to meet you\" is **Mucho gusto** (*MOO-choh GOOS-toh*). You can also say **encantado** (male speaker) or **encantada** (female speaker)."],
  ["how do you say see you later in spanish | see you later in spanish | spanish for see you later", "In Spanish, \"see you later\" is **Hasta luego** (*AHS-tah LWEH-goh*). See you tomorrow is **hasta mañana**."],
  ["count to ten in spanish | how do you count to 10 in spanish | numbers 1 to 10 in spanish", "Counting to ten in Spanish:\n1 — **uno** (*OO-noh*)\n2 — **dos** (*dohs*)\n3 — **tres** (*trehs*)\n4 — **cuatro** (*KWAH-troh*)\n5 — **cinco** (*SEEN-koh*)\n6 — **seis** (*says*)\n7 — **siete** (*see-EH-teh*)\n8 — **ocho** (*OH-choh*)\n9 — **nueve** (*NWEH-veh*)\n10 — **diez** (*dee-EHS*)"],
  ["days of the week in spanish | how do you say monday in spanish | spanish days of the week", "The days of the week in Spanish:\n• Monday — **lunes**\n• Tuesday — **martes**\n• Wednesday — **miércoles**\n• Thursday — **jueves**\n• Friday — **viernes**\n• Saturday — **sábado**\n• Sunday — **domingo**\nSpanish doesn't capitalize the days of the week."],
  ["colors in spanish | colours in spanish | how do you say red in spanish", "Colors in Spanish:\n• Red — **rojo**\n• Orange — **naranja**\n• Yellow — **amarillo**\n• Green — **verde**\n• Blue — **azul**\n• Purple — **morado**\n• Black — **negro**\n• White — **blanco**\nColors usually come after the noun and change for gender: *una casa roja* (a red house)."],
  ["how do you say good morning in french | good morning in french | french for good morning", "In French, good morning is **Bonjour** (*bohn-ZHOOR*). French uses **bonjour** for both \"hello\" and \"good morning\", all day until the evening."],
  ["how do you say good night in french | good night in french | goodnight in french", "In French, good night is **Bonne nuit** (*bun NWEE*). When you meet someone in the evening, say **bonsoir** (*bohn-SWAHR*, good evening) instead."],
  ["how do you say how are you in french | how are you in french | french for how are you", "In French, \"how are you?\" is **Comment ça va ?** (*koh-mahn sah VAH*). Casual: **Ça va ?** Polite: **Comment allez-vous ?** Reply: **Ça va bien, merci.**"],
  ["how do you say my name is in french | my name is in french | what is your name in french", "In French, \"my name is …\" is **Je m'appelle …** (*zhuh mah-PELL*) — just add your name. To ask: **Comment tu t'appelles ?** (casual) or **Comment vous appelez-vous ?** (polite)."],
  ["how do you say i love you in french | i love you in french | french for i love you", "In French, \"I love you\" is **Je t'aime** (*zhuh TEM*). It's used with family as well as sweethearts — *Je t'aime, maman!*"],
  ["how do you say happy birthday in french | happy birthday in french | french for happy birthday", "In French, \"happy birthday\" is **Joyeux anniversaire !** (*zhwah-YUH zah-nee-vehr-SEHR*). In Québec people also say **Bonne fête !**"],
  ["how do you say sorry in french | how do you say excuse me in french | sorry in french | excuse me in french", "In French, \"excuse me\" is **Excusez-moi** (*ex-kew-zay-MWAH*) and \"sorry\" is **Pardon / Désolé** (*par-DOHN / day-zoh-LAY*). A female speaker writes **désolée** (it sounds the same)."],
  ["how do you say where is the bathroom in french | where is the bathroom in french | where is the toilet in french", "In French, \"where is the bathroom?\" is **Où sont les toilettes ?** (*oo sohn lay twah-LET*)."],
  ["how do you say i don't understand in french | i don't understand in french | i dont understand in french", "In French, \"I don't understand\" is **Je ne comprends pas** (*zhuh nuh kohm-prahn PAH*)."],
  ["how do you say do you speak english in french | do you speak english in french | how to ask if someone speaks english in french", "In French, \"do you speak English?\" is **Parlez-vous anglais ?** (*par-lay voo ahn-GLAY*)."],
  ["how do you say how much is this in french | how much is this in french | how much does it cost in french", "In French, \"how much is this?\" is **C'est combien ?** (*say kohm-BYAN*). Also: **Combien ça coûte ?**"],
  ["how do you say nice to meet you in french | nice to meet you in french | french for nice to meet you", "In French, \"nice to meet you\" is **Enchanté** (*ahn-shahn-TAY*). A female speaker writes **enchantée** (same sound)."],
  ["how do you say see you later in french | see you later in french | french for see you later", "In French, \"see you later\" is **À plus tard** (*ah plew TAR*). Casual: **À plus !** or **À tout à l'heure !** (see you in a bit)."],
  ["count to ten in french | how do you count to 10 in french | numbers 1 to 10 in french", "Counting to ten in French:\n1 — **un** (*uhn*)\n2 — **deux** (*duh*)\n3 — **trois** (*trwah*)\n4 — **quatre** (*KAH-truh*)\n5 — **cinq** (*sank*)\n6 — **six** (*sees*)\n7 — **sept** (*set*)\n8 — **huit** (*weet*)\n9 — **neuf** (*nuhf*)\n10 — **dix** (*dees*)"],
  ["days of the week in french | how do you say monday in french | french days of the week", "The days of the week in French:\n• Monday — **lundi**\n• Tuesday — **mardi**\n• Wednesday — **mercredi**\n• Thursday — **jeudi**\n• Friday — **vendredi**\n• Saturday — **samedi**\n• Sunday — **dimanche**\nFrench doesn't capitalize the days. The week starts on Monday."],
  ["colors in french | colours in french | how do you say red in french", "Colors in French:\n• Red — **rouge**\n• Orange — **orange**\n• Yellow — **jaune**\n• Green — **vert**\n• Blue — **bleu**\n• Purple — **violet**\n• Black — **noir**\n• White — **blanc**\nColors usually go after the noun: *une pomme rouge* (a red apple)."],
  ["how do you say good morning in german | good morning in german | german for good morning", "In German, good morning is **Guten Morgen** (*GOO-ten MOR-gen*). Casual: just **Morgen!**"],
  ["how do you say good night in german | good night in german | goodnight in german", "In German, good night is **Gute Nacht** (*GOO-tuh NAHKT*). Good evening is **Guten Abend**."],
  ["how do you say how are you in german | how are you in german | german for how are you", "In German, \"how are you?\" is **Wie geht es dir?** (*vee GAYT es deer*). Polite: **Wie geht es Ihnen?** Casual: **Wie geht's?** Reply: **Gut, danke!**"],
  ["how do you say my name is in german | my name is in german | what is your name in german", "In German, \"my name is …\" is **Ich heiße …** (*ikh HY-suh*) — just add your name. To ask: **Wie heißt du?** (casual) or **Wie heißen Sie?** (polite)."],
  ["how do you say i love you in german | i love you in german | german for i love you", "In German, \"I love you\" is **Ich liebe dich** (*ikh LEE-buh dikh*). For family and friends, Germans often say **Ich hab dich lieb** (I'm really fond of you)."],
  ["how do you say happy birthday in german | happy birthday in german | german for happy birthday", "In German, \"happy birthday\" is **Alles Gute zum Geburtstag!** (*AH-les GOO-tuh tsoom geh-BOORTS-tahk*)."],
  ["how do you say sorry in german | how do you say excuse me in german | sorry in german | excuse me in german", "In German, \"excuse me\" is **Entschuldigung** (*ent-SHOOL-dee-goong*) and \"sorry\" is **Es tut mir leid** (*es toot meer LITE*). **Entschuldigung** also works as a quick \"sorry\"."],
  ["how do you say where is the bathroom in german | where is the bathroom in german | where is the toilet in german", "In German, \"where is the bathroom?\" is **Wo ist die Toilette?** (*voh ist dee toy-LET-uh*)."],
  ["how do you say i don't understand in german | i don't understand in german | i dont understand in german", "In German, \"I don't understand\" is **Ich verstehe nicht** (*ikh fer-SHTAY-uh nikht*)."],
  ["how do you say do you speak english in german | do you speak english in german | how to ask if someone speaks english in german", "In German, \"do you speak English?\" is **Sprechen Sie Englisch?** (*SHPREKH-en zee ENG-lish*). Casual: **Sprichst du Englisch?**"],
  ["how do you say how much is this in german | how much is this in german | how much does it cost in german", "In German, \"how much is this?\" is **Wie viel kostet das?** (*vee feel KOS-tet dahs*)."],
  ["how do you say nice to meet you in german | nice to meet you in german | german for nice to meet you", "In German, \"nice to meet you\" is **Freut mich** (*froyt mikh*). Longer and polite: **Freut mich, Sie kennenzulernen.**"],
  ["how do you say see you later in german | see you later in german | german for see you later", "In German, \"see you later\" is **Bis später** (*bis SHPAY-ter*). Also **Bis bald** (see you soon)."],
  ["count to ten in german | how do you count to 10 in german | numbers 1 to 10 in german", "Counting to ten in German:\n1 — **eins** (*eyns*)\n2 — **zwei** (*tsvy*)\n3 — **drei** (*dry*)\n4 — **vier** (*feer*)\n5 — **fünf** (*fewnf*)\n6 — **sechs** (*zeks*)\n7 — **sieben** (*ZEE-ben*)\n8 — **acht** (*ahkt*)\n9 — **neun** (*noyn*)\n10 — **zehn** (*tsayn*)"],
  ["days of the week in german | how do you say monday in german | german days of the week", "The days of the week in German:\n• Monday — **Montag**\n• Tuesday — **Dienstag**\n• Wednesday — **Mittwoch**\n• Thursday — **Donnerstag**\n• Friday — **Freitag**\n• Saturday — **Samstag**\n• Sunday — **Sonntag**\n*Mittwoch* literally means \"mid-week\"."],
  ["colors in german | colours in german | how do you say red in german", "Colors in German:\n• Red — **rot**\n• Orange — **orange**\n• Yellow — **gelb**\n• Green — **grün**\n• Blue — **blau**\n• Purple — **lila**\n• Black — **schwarz**\n• White — **weiß**"],
  ["how do you say good morning in italian | good morning in italian | italian for good morning", "In Italian, good morning is **Buongiorno** (*bwon-JOR-noh*). It also means \"good day\" and works until the afternoon."],
  ["how do you say good night in italian | good night in italian | goodnight in italian", "In Italian, good night is **Buonanotte** (*bwoh-nah-NOT-teh*). Good evening is **buonasera**."],
  ["how do you say how are you in italian | how are you in italian | italian for how are you", "In Italian, \"how are you?\" is **Come stai?** (*KOH-meh STY*). Polite: **Come sta?** Reply: **Bene, grazie!**"],
  ["how do you say my name is in italian | my name is in italian | what is your name in italian", "In Italian, \"my name is …\" is **Mi chiamo …** (*mee kee-AH-moh*) — just add your name. To ask: **Come ti chiami?** (*KOH-meh tee kee-AH-mee*)"],
  ["how do you say i love you in italian | i love you in italian | italian for i love you", "In Italian, \"I love you\" is **Ti voglio bene** (*tee VOL-yoh BEH-neh*). This is the warm \"I love you\" for family and friends. **Ti amo** is for romantic love."],
  ["how do you say happy birthday in italian | happy birthday in italian | italian for happy birthday", "In Italian, \"happy birthday\" is **Buon compleanno!** (*bwon kom-pleh-AHN-noh*). Also: **Tanti auguri!** (best wishes!)"],
  ["how do you say sorry in italian | how do you say excuse me in italian | sorry in italian | excuse me in italian", "In Italian, \"excuse me\" is **Mi scusi** (*mee SKOO-zee*) and \"sorry\" is **Mi dispiace** (*mee dee-SPYAH-cheh*). With friends, a quick **scusa!** works for both."],
  ["how do you say where is the bathroom in italian | where is the bathroom in italian | where is the toilet in italian", "In Italian, \"where is the bathroom?\" is **Dov'è il bagno?** (*doh-VEH eel BAHN-yoh*)."],
  ["how do you say i don't understand in italian | i don't understand in italian | i dont understand in italian", "In Italian, \"I don't understand\" is **Non capisco** (*nohn kah-PEES-koh*)."],
  ["how do you say do you speak english in italian | do you speak english in italian | how to ask if someone speaks english in italian", "In Italian, \"do you speak English?\" is **Parla inglese?** (*PAR-lah een-GLEH-zeh*). Casual: **Parli inglese?**"],
  ["how do you say how much is this in italian | how much is this in italian | how much does it cost in italian", "In Italian, \"how much is this?\" is **Quanto costa?** (*KWAN-toh KOS-tah*)."],
  ["how do you say nice to meet you in italian | nice to meet you in italian | italian for nice to meet you", "In Italian, \"nice to meet you\" is **Piacere** (*pyah-CHEH-reh*). Longer: **Piacere di conoscerti.**"],
  ["how do you say see you later in italian | see you later in italian | italian for see you later", "In Italian, \"see you later\" is **A dopo** (*ah DOH-poh*). Also **Ci vediamo!** (see you!)."],
  ["count to ten in italian | how do you count to 10 in italian | numbers 1 to 10 in italian", "Counting to ten in Italian:\n1 — **uno** (*OO-noh*)\n2 — **due** (*DOO-eh*)\n3 — **tre** (*treh*)\n4 — **quattro** (*KWAHT-troh*)\n5 — **cinque** (*CHEEN-kweh*)\n6 — **sei** (*say*)\n7 — **sette** (*SET-teh*)\n8 — **otto** (*OHT-toh*)\n9 — **nove** (*NOH-veh*)\n10 — **dieci** (*DYEH-chee*)"],
  ["days of the week in italian | how do you say monday in italian | italian days of the week", "The days of the week in Italian:\n• Monday — **lunedì**\n• Tuesday — **martedì**\n• Wednesday — **mercoledì**\n• Thursday — **giovedì**\n• Friday — **venerdì**\n• Saturday — **sabato**\n• Sunday — **domenica**\nItalian doesn't capitalize the days."],
  ["colors in italian | colours in italian | how do you say red in italian", "Colors in Italian:\n• Red — **rosso**\n• Orange — **arancione**\n• Yellow — **giallo**\n• Green — **verde**\n• Blue — **blu**\n• Purple — **viola**\n• Black — **nero**\n• White — **bianco**\nLight blue has its own word: **azzurro** — the color of Italy's national sports teams."],
  ["how do you say good morning in portuguese | good morning in portuguese | portuguese for good morning", "In Portuguese, good morning is **Bom dia** (*bohm DEE-ah*)."],
  ["how do you say good night in portuguese | good night in portuguese | goodnight in portuguese", "In Portuguese, good night is **Boa noite** (*BOH-ah NOY-chee*). (In Portugal it sounds more like *NOY-tuh*.) It also means good evening."],
  ["how do you say how are you in portuguese | how are you in portuguese | portuguese for how are you", "In Portuguese, \"how are you?\" is **Tudo bem?** (*TOO-doo bayn*). Also **Como vai?** or **Como está?** The usual reply is **Tudo bem!**"],
  ["how do you say my name is in portuguese | my name is in portuguese | what is your name in portuguese", "In Portuguese, \"my name is …\" is **Meu nome é …** (*MEH-oo NOH-mee eh*) — just add your name. Also **Eu me chamo …** (Brazil) or **Chamo-me …** (Portugal). To ask: **Qual é o seu nome?**"],
  ["how do you say i love you in portuguese | i love you in portuguese | portuguese for i love you", "In Portuguese, \"I love you\" is **Eu te amo** (*EH-oo chee AH-moo*). That's Brazilian Portuguese; in Portugal people say **Amo-te**. Both are said to family, too."],
  ["how do you say happy birthday in portuguese | happy birthday in portuguese | portuguese for happy birthday", "In Portuguese, \"happy birthday\" is **Feliz aniversário!** (*feh-LEES ah-nee-ver-SAH-ree-oo*). People also just say **Parabéns!** (congratulations!)."],
  ["how do you say sorry in portuguese | how do you say excuse me in portuguese | sorry in portuguese | excuse me in portuguese", "In Portuguese, \"excuse me\" is **Com licença** (*kohn lee-SEN-sah*) and \"sorry\" is **Desculpe** (*dehs-KOOL-pee*)."],
  ["how do you say where is the bathroom in portuguese | where is the bathroom in portuguese | where is the toilet in portuguese", "In Portuguese, \"where is the bathroom?\" is **Onde fica o banheiro?** (*OHN-jee FEE-kah oo bahn-YAY-roo*). That's Brazilian. In Portugal ask **Onde é a casa de banho?**"],
  ["how do you say i don't understand in portuguese | i don't understand in portuguese | i dont understand in portuguese", "In Portuguese, \"I don't understand\" is **Não entendo** (*nowng en-TEN-doo*). Also **Não entendi** (I didn't understand)."],
  ["how do you say do you speak english in portuguese | do you speak english in portuguese | how to ask if someone speaks english in portuguese", "In Portuguese, \"do you speak English?\" is **Você fala inglês?** (*voh-SAY FAH-lah een-GLAYS*)."],
  ["how do you say how much is this in portuguese | how much is this in portuguese | how much does it cost in portuguese", "In Portuguese, \"how much is this?\" is **Quanto custa?** (*KWAN-too KOOS-tah*)."],
  ["how do you say nice to meet you in portuguese | nice to meet you in portuguese | portuguese for nice to meet you", "In Portuguese, \"nice to meet you\" is **Muito prazer** (*MWEE-too prah-ZEHR*). Short: **Prazer!**"],
  ["how do you say see you later in portuguese | see you later in portuguese | portuguese for see you later", "In Portuguese, \"see you later\" is **Até logo** (*ah-TEH LOH-goo*). Also **Até mais!**"],
  ["count to ten in portuguese | how do you count to 10 in portuguese | numbers 1 to 10 in portuguese", "Counting to ten in Portuguese:\n1 — **um**\n2 — **dois**\n3 — **três**\n4 — **quatro**\n5 — **cinco**\n6 — **seis**\n7 — **sete**\n8 — **oito**\n9 — **nove**\n10 — **dez**\nIn Brazil people often say **meia** for six when reading out phone numbers."],
  ["days of the week in portuguese | how do you say monday in portuguese | portuguese days of the week", "The days of the week in Portuguese:\n• Monday — **segunda-feira**\n• Tuesday — **terça-feira**\n• Wednesday — **quarta-feira**\n• Thursday — **quinta-feira**\n• Friday — **sexta-feira**\n• Saturday — **sábado**\n• Sunday — **domingo**\nThe weekdays literally mean \"second day\", \"third day\" and so on, and are often shortened to *segunda*, *terça*…"],
  ["colors in portuguese | colours in portuguese | how do you say red in portuguese", "Colors in Portuguese:\n• Red — **vermelho**\n• Orange — **laranja**\n• Yellow — **amarelo**\n• Green — **verde**\n• Blue — **azul**\n• Purple — **roxo**\n• Black — **preto**\n• White — **branco**"],
  ["how do you say good morning in dutch | good morning in dutch | dutch for good morning", "In Dutch, good morning is **Goedemorgen** (*KHOO-duh-mor-khun*). The Dutch *g* is a throaty sound, a bit like clearing your throat."],
  ["how do you say good night in dutch | good night in dutch | goodnight in dutch", "In Dutch, good night is **Welterusten** (*vel-tuh-RUS-tun*). Literally \"rest well\". **Goedenacht** also works."],
  ["how do you say how are you in dutch | how are you in dutch | dutch for how are you", "In Dutch, \"how are you?\" is **Hoe gaat het?** (*hoo KHAHT ut*). Reply: **Goed, dank je!**"],
  ["how do you say my name is in dutch | my name is in dutch | what is your name in dutch", "In Dutch, \"my name is …\" is **Ik heet …** (*ik HAYT*) — just add your name. To ask: **Hoe heet je?**"],
  ["how do you say i love you in dutch | i love you in dutch | dutch for i love you", "In Dutch, \"I love you\" is **Ik hou van jou** (*ik how fun YOW*)."],
  ["how do you say happy birthday in dutch | happy birthday in dutch | dutch for happy birthday", "In Dutch, \"happy birthday\" is **Gefeliciteerd!** (*khuh-fay-lee-see-TAYRT*). Also **Fijne verjaardag!** Fun fact: in the Netherlands people congratulate the birthday person's family too!"],
  ["how do you say sorry in dutch | how do you say excuse me in dutch | sorry in dutch | excuse me in dutch", "In Dutch, \"excuse me\" is **Pardon** (*par-DON*) and \"sorry\" is **Sorry / Het spijt me** (*SOR-ee / ut SPAYT muh*)."],
  ["how do you say where is the bathroom in dutch | where is the bathroom in dutch | where is the toilet in dutch", "In Dutch, \"where is the bathroom?\" is **Waar is het toilet?** (*vahr is ut twah-LET*)."],
  ["how do you say i don't understand in dutch | i don't understand in dutch | i dont understand in dutch", "In Dutch, \"I don't understand\" is **Ik begrijp het niet** (*ik buh-KHRAYP ut neet*)."],
  ["how do you say do you speak english in dutch | do you speak english in dutch | how to ask if someone speaks english in dutch", "In Dutch, \"do you speak English?\" is **Spreekt u Engels?** (*spraykt ew ENG-uls*). Casual: **Spreek je Engels?** (Most Dutch people do!)"],
  ["how do you say how much is this in dutch | how much is this in dutch | how much does it cost in dutch", "In Dutch, \"how much is this?\" is **Hoeveel kost dit?** (*hoo-FAYL kost dit*)."],
  ["how do you say nice to meet you in dutch | nice to meet you in dutch | dutch for nice to meet you", "In Dutch, \"nice to meet you\" is **Leuk je te ontmoeten** (*lurk yuh tuh ont-MOO-tun*). Formal: **Aangenaam.**"],
  ["how do you say see you later in dutch | see you later in dutch | dutch for see you later", "In Dutch, \"see you later\" is **Tot later** (*tot LAH-ter*). Also **Tot straks** (see you soon)."],
  ["count to ten in dutch | how do you count to 10 in dutch | numbers 1 to 10 in dutch", "Counting to ten in Dutch:\n1 — **een**\n2 — **twee**\n3 — **drie**\n4 — **vier**\n5 — **vijf**\n6 — **zes**\n7 — **zeven**\n8 — **acht**\n9 — **negen**\n10 — **tien**"],
  ["days of the week in dutch | how do you say monday in dutch | dutch days of the week", "The days of the week in Dutch:\n• Monday — **maandag**\n• Tuesday — **dinsdag**\n• Wednesday — **woensdag**\n• Thursday — **donderdag**\n• Friday — **vrijdag**\n• Saturday — **zaterdag**\n• Sunday — **zondag**"],
  ["colors in dutch | colours in dutch | how do you say red in dutch", "Colors in Dutch:\n• Red — **rood**\n• Orange — **oranje**\n• Yellow — **geel**\n• Green — **groen**\n• Blue — **blauw**\n• Purple — **paars**\n• Black — **zwart**\n• White — **wit**\nOrange (*oranje*) is the Netherlands' national color, after the royal House of Orange."],
  ["how do you say good morning in swedish | good morning in swedish | swedish for good morning", "In Swedish, good morning is **God morgon** (*goo MOR-on*)."],
  ["how do you say good night in swedish | good night in swedish | goodnight in swedish", "In Swedish, good night is **God natt** (*goo NAHT*)."],
  ["how do you say how are you in swedish | how are you in swedish | swedish for how are you", "In Swedish, \"how are you?\" is **Hur mår du?** (*hoor mor doo*). Reply: **Bra, tack!** (Good, thanks!)"],
  ["how do you say my name is in swedish | my name is in swedish | what is your name in swedish", "In Swedish, \"my name is …\" is **Jag heter …** (*yah HEH-ter*) — just add your name. To ask: **Vad heter du?**"],
  ["how do you say i love you in swedish | i love you in swedish | swedish for i love you", "In Swedish, \"I love you\" is **Jag älskar dig** (*yah EL-skar day*)."],
  ["how do you say happy birthday in swedish | happy birthday in swedish | swedish for happy birthday", "In Swedish, \"happy birthday\" is **Grattis på födelsedagen!** (*GRAH-tis poh FUR-del-seh-dah-gen*). Short: **Grattis!**"],
  ["how do you say sorry in swedish | how do you say excuse me in swedish | sorry in swedish | excuse me in swedish", "In Swedish, \"excuse me\" is **Ursäkta** (*OOR-shek-tah*) and \"sorry\" is **Förlåt** (*fur-LOHT*)."],
  ["how do you say where is the bathroom in swedish | where is the bathroom in swedish | where is the toilet in swedish", "In Swedish, \"where is the bathroom?\" is **Var är toaletten?** (*vahr air too-ah-LET-en*)."],
  ["how do you say i don't understand in swedish | i don't understand in swedish | i dont understand in swedish", "In Swedish, \"I don't understand\" is **Jag förstår inte** (*yah fur-STOHR IN-teh*)."],
  ["how do you say do you speak english in swedish | do you speak english in swedish | how to ask if someone speaks english in swedish", "In Swedish, \"do you speak English?\" is **Talar du engelska?** (*TAH-lar doo ENG-el-skah*)."],
  ["how do you say how much is this in swedish | how much is this in swedish | how much does it cost in swedish", "In Swedish, \"how much is this?\" is **Hur mycket kostar det?** (*hoor MUK-eh KOS-tar deh*)."],
  ["how do you say nice to meet you in swedish | nice to meet you in swedish | swedish for nice to meet you", "In Swedish, \"nice to meet you\" is **Trevligt att träffas** (*TREV-lit at TREF-as*)."],
  ["how do you say see you later in swedish | see you later in swedish | swedish for see you later", "In Swedish, \"see you later\" is **Vi ses senare** (*vee SAYS SEH-nah-reh*). Short: **Vi ses!** (See you!)"],
  ["count to ten in swedish | how do you count to 10 in swedish | numbers 1 to 10 in swedish", "Counting to ten in Swedish:\n1 — **ett**\n2 — **två**\n3 — **tre**\n4 — **fyra**\n5 — **fem**\n6 — **sex**\n7 — **sju**\n8 — **åtta**\n9 — **nio**\n10 — **tio**"],
  ["days of the week in swedish | how do you say monday in swedish | swedish days of the week", "The days of the week in Swedish:\n• Monday — **måndag**\n• Tuesday — **tisdag**\n• Wednesday — **onsdag**\n• Thursday — **torsdag**\n• Friday — **fredag**\n• Saturday — **lördag**\n• Sunday — **söndag**\n*Torsdag* is named after the god Thor, just like English *Thursday*."],
  ["colors in swedish | colours in swedish | how do you say red in swedish", "Colors in Swedish:\n• Red — **röd**\n• Orange — **orange**\n• Yellow — **gul**\n• Green — **grön**\n• Blue — **blå**\n• Purple — **lila**\n• Black — **svart**\n• White — **vit**\nBlue and yellow (*blå och gul*) are the colors of the Swedish flag."],
  ["how do you say good morning in norwegian | good morning in norwegian | norwegian for good morning", "In Norwegian, good morning is **God morgen** (*goo MOR-en*)."],
  ["how do you say good night in norwegian | good night in norwegian | goodnight in norwegian", "In Norwegian, good night is **God natt** (*goo NAHT*)."],
  ["how do you say how are you in norwegian | how are you in norwegian | norwegian for how are you", "In Norwegian, \"how are you?\" is **Hvordan har du det?** (*VOOR-dahn har doo deh*). Reply: **Bra, takk!**"],
  ["how do you say my name is in norwegian | my name is in norwegian | what is your name in norwegian", "In Norwegian, \"my name is …\" is **Jeg heter …** (*yai HAY-ter*) — just add your name. To ask: **Hva heter du?**"],
  ["how do you say i love you in norwegian | i love you in norwegian | norwegian for i love you", "In Norwegian, \"I love you\" is **Jeg elsker deg** (*yai ELS-ker dai*)."],
  ["how do you say happy birthday in norwegian | happy birthday in norwegian | norwegian for happy birthday", "In Norwegian, \"happy birthday\" is **Gratulerer med dagen!** (*grah-too-LEH-rer meh DAH-gen*). Literally \"congratulations on the day\"."],
  ["how do you say sorry in norwegian | how do you say excuse me in norwegian | sorry in norwegian | excuse me in norwegian", "In Norwegian, \"excuse me\" is **Unnskyld** (*UN-shyld*) and \"sorry\" is **Beklager** (*beh-KLAH-ger*). **Unnskyld** also works as a quick \"sorry\"."],
  ["how do you say where is the bathroom in norwegian | where is the bathroom in norwegian | where is the toilet in norwegian", "In Norwegian, \"where is the bathroom?\" is **Hvor er toalettet?** (*voor ar too-ah-LET-teh*)."],
  ["how do you say i don't understand in norwegian | i don't understand in norwegian | i dont understand in norwegian", "In Norwegian, \"I don't understand\" is **Jeg forstår ikke** (*yai for-STOHR IK-keh*)."],
  ["how do you say do you speak english in norwegian | do you speak english in norwegian | how to ask if someone speaks english in norwegian", "In Norwegian, \"do you speak English?\" is **Snakker du engelsk?** (*SNAHK-ker doo ENG-elsk*)."],
  ["how do you say how much is this in norwegian | how much is this in norwegian | how much does it cost in norwegian", "In Norwegian, \"how much is this?\" is **Hvor mye koster dette?** (*voor MEE-eh KOS-ter DET-teh*)."],
  ["how do you say nice to meet you in norwegian | nice to meet you in norwegian | norwegian for nice to meet you", "In Norwegian, \"nice to meet you\" is **Hyggelig å møte deg** (*HUG-geh-lee oh MUR-teh dai*)."],
  ["how do you say see you later in norwegian | see you later in norwegian | norwegian for see you later", "In Norwegian, \"see you later\" is **Vi ses senere** (*vee SAYS SEH-neh-reh*). Short: **Vi ses!**"],
  ["count to ten in norwegian | how do you count to 10 in norwegian | numbers 1 to 10 in norwegian", "Counting to ten in Norwegian:\n1 — **én**\n2 — **to**\n3 — **tre**\n4 — **fire**\n5 — **fem**\n6 — **seks**\n7 — **sju**\n8 — **åtte**\n9 — **ni**\n10 — **ti**"],
  ["days of the week in norwegian | how do you say monday in norwegian | norwegian days of the week", "The days of the week in Norwegian:\n• Monday — **mandag**\n• Tuesday — **tirsdag**\n• Wednesday — **onsdag**\n• Thursday — **torsdag**\n• Friday — **fredag**\n• Saturday — **lørdag**\n• Sunday — **søndag**"],
  ["colors in norwegian | colours in norwegian | how do you say red in norwegian", "Colors in Norwegian:\n• Red — **rød**\n• Orange — **oransje**\n• Yellow — **gul**\n• Green — **grønn**\n• Blue — **blå**\n• Purple — **lilla**\n• Black — **svart**\n• White — **hvit**\nThese are in Bokmål, the most common way of writing Norwegian."],
  ["how do you say good morning in danish | good morning in danish | danish for good morning", "In Danish, good morning is **Godmorgen** (*goh-MORN*)."],
  ["how do you say good night in danish | good night in danish | goodnight in danish", "In Danish, good night is **Godnat** (*goh-NAT*)."],
  ["how do you say how are you in danish | how are you in danish | danish for how are you", "In Danish, \"how are you?\" is **Hvordan har du det?** (*VOR-dan har doo deh*). Reply: **Godt, tak!**"],
  ["how do you say my name is in danish | my name is in danish | what is your name in danish", "In Danish, \"my name is …\" is **Jeg hedder …** (*yai HEH-ther*) — just add your name. To ask: **Hvad hedder du?**"],
  ["how do you say i love you in danish | i love you in danish | danish for i love you", "In Danish, \"I love you\" is **Jeg elsker dig** (*yai EL-sker dai*)."],
  ["how do you say happy birthday in danish | happy birthday in danish | danish for happy birthday", "In Danish, \"happy birthday\" is **Tillykke med fødselsdagen!** (*til-LUK-keh meh FUSS-els-day-en*). Short: **Tillykke!**"],
  ["how do you say sorry in danish | how do you say excuse me in danish | sorry in danish | excuse me in danish", "In Danish, **Undskyld** (*UN-skool*) means both \"excuse me\" and \"sorry\". To show sympathy (\"I'm so sorry\"), say **Det er jeg ked af** (*deh air yai KETH ah*)."],
  ["how do you say where is the bathroom in danish | where is the bathroom in danish | where is the toilet in danish", "In Danish, \"where is the bathroom?\" is **Hvor er toilettet?** (*vor air toy-LET-teth*)."],
  ["how do you say i don't understand in danish | i don't understand in danish | i dont understand in danish", "In Danish, \"I don't understand\" is **Jeg forstår ikke** (*yai for-STOR IG-geh*)."],
  ["how do you say do you speak english in danish | do you speak english in danish | how to ask if someone speaks english in danish", "In Danish, \"do you speak English?\" is **Taler du engelsk?** (*TAY-ler doo ENG-elsk*)."],
  ["how do you say how much is this in danish | how much is this in danish | how much does it cost in danish", "In Danish, \"how much is this?\" is **Hvor meget koster det?** (*vor MY-et KOS-ter deh*)."],
  ["how do you say nice to meet you in danish | nice to meet you in danish | danish for nice to meet you", "In Danish, \"nice to meet you\" is **Hyggeligt at møde dig** (*HYOO-geh-lit at MUR-the dai*)."],
  ["how do you say see you later in danish | see you later in danish | danish for see you later", "In Danish, \"see you later\" is **Vi ses senere** (*vee SAYS SEH-neh-reh*). Short: **Vi ses!**"],
  ["count to ten in danish | how do you count to 10 in danish | numbers 1 to 10 in danish", "Counting to ten in Danish:\n1 — **en**\n2 — **to**\n3 — **tre**\n4 — **fire**\n5 — **fem**\n6 — **seks**\n7 — **syv**\n8 — **otte**\n9 — **ni**\n10 — **ti**"],
  ["days of the week in danish | how do you say monday in danish | danish days of the week", "The days of the week in Danish:\n• Monday — **mandag**\n• Tuesday — **tirsdag**\n• Wednesday — **onsdag**\n• Thursday — **torsdag**\n• Friday — **fredag**\n• Saturday — **lørdag**\n• Sunday — **søndag**"],
  ["colors in danish | colours in danish | how do you say red in danish", "Colors in Danish:\n• Red — **rød**\n• Orange — **orange**\n• Yellow — **gul**\n• Green — **grøn**\n• Blue — **blå**\n• Purple — **lilla**\n• Black — **sort**\n• White — **hvid**\nRed and white (*rød og hvid*) are the colors of the Danish flag, one of the oldest in the world."],
  ["how do you say good morning in finnish | good morning in finnish | finnish for good morning", "In Finnish, good morning is **Hyvää huomenta** (*HU-vaa HWOH-men-tah*)."],
  ["how do you say good night in finnish | good night in finnish | goodnight in finnish", "In Finnish, good night is **Hyvää yötä** (*HU-vaa EW-uh-tah*)."],
  ["how do you say how are you in finnish | how are you in finnish | finnish for how are you", "In Finnish, \"how are you?\" is **Mitä kuuluu?** (*MI-ta KOO-loo*). Reply: **Hyvää, kiitos!** (Fine, thanks!)"],
  ["how do you say my name is in finnish | my name is in finnish | what is your name in finnish", "In Finnish, \"my name is …\" is **Minun nimeni on …** (*MI-noon NI-meh-ni on*) — just add your name. Casual: **Olen …** (I am …). To ask: **Mikä sinun nimesi on?**"],
  ["how do you say i love you in finnish | i love you in finnish | finnish for i love you", "In Finnish, \"I love you\" is **Minä rakastan sinua** (*MI-na RAH-kahs-tahn SI-noo-ah*). Shorter: **Rakastan sinua.**"],
  ["how do you say happy birthday in finnish | happy birthday in finnish | finnish for happy birthday", "In Finnish, \"happy birthday\" is **Hyvää syntymäpäivää!** (*HU-vaa SUN-tu-ma-pai-vaa*). People also say **Paljon onnea!** (lots of happiness!)."],
  ["how do you say sorry in finnish | how do you say excuse me in finnish | sorry in finnish | excuse me in finnish", "In Finnish, **Anteeksi** (*AHN-tayk-si*) means both \"excuse me\" and \"sorry\". For a bigger apology: **Olen pahoillani** (*O-len PAH-hoil-lah-ni*, I'm sorry)."],
  ["how do you say where is the bathroom in finnish | where is the bathroom in finnish | where is the toilet in finnish", "In Finnish, \"where is the bathroom?\" is **Missä on vessa?** (*MIS-sa on VES-sah*)."],
  ["how do you say i don't understand in finnish | i don't understand in finnish | i dont understand in finnish", "In Finnish, \"I don't understand\" is **En ymmärrä** (*en UM-mar-ra*)."],
  ["how do you say do you speak english in finnish | do you speak english in finnish | how to ask if someone speaks english in finnish", "In Finnish, \"do you speak English?\" is **Puhutko englantia?** (*PU-hut-ko ENG-lahn-ti-ah*)."],
  ["how do you say how much is this in finnish | how much is this in finnish | how much does it cost in finnish", "In Finnish, \"how much is this?\" is **Paljonko tämä maksaa?** (*PAHL-yon-ko TA-ma MAHK-saa*)."],
  ["how do you say nice to meet you in finnish | nice to meet you in finnish | finnish for nice to meet you", "In Finnish, \"nice to meet you\" is **Hauska tavata** (*HOW-skah TAH-vah-tah*)."],
  ["how do you say see you later in finnish | see you later in finnish | finnish for see you later", "In Finnish, \"see you later\" is **Nähdään myöhemmin** (*NAH-daan MYUR-hem-min*). Short: **Nähdään!** (See you!)"],
  ["count to ten in finnish | how do you count to 10 in finnish | numbers 1 to 10 in finnish", "Counting to ten in Finnish:\n1 — **yksi**\n2 — **kaksi**\n3 — **kolme**\n4 — **neljä**\n5 — **viisi**\n6 — **kuusi**\n7 — **seitsemän**\n8 — **kahdeksan**\n9 — **yhdeksän**\n10 — **kymmenen**\nFinnish is spelled the way it sounds — always stress the first syllable."],
  ["days of the week in finnish | how do you say monday in finnish | finnish days of the week", "The days of the week in Finnish:\n• Monday — **maanantai**\n• Tuesday — **tiistai**\n• Wednesday — **keskiviikko**\n• Thursday — **torstai**\n• Friday — **perjantai**\n• Saturday — **lauantai**\n• Sunday — **sunnuntai**\n*Keskiviikko* (Wednesday) means \"mid-week\"."],
  ["colors in finnish | colours in finnish | how do you say red in finnish", "Colors in Finnish:\n• Red — **punainen**\n• Orange — **oranssi**\n• Yellow — **keltainen**\n• Green — **vihreä**\n• Blue — **sininen**\n• Purple — **violetti**\n• Black — **musta**\n• White — **valkoinen**"],
  ["how do you say good morning in polish | good morning in polish | polish for good morning", "In Polish, good morning is **Dzień dobry** (*jen DOH-bri*). Poles use it all day as \"hello / good day\"."],
  ["how do you say good night in polish | good night in polish | goodnight in polish", "In Polish, good night is **Dobranoc** (*doh-BRAH-nots*). Good evening is **dobry wieczór**."],
  ["how do you say how are you in polish | how are you in polish | polish for how are you", "In Polish, \"how are you?\" is **Jak się masz?** (*yahk sheh MAHSH*). Reply: **Dobrze, dziękuję!** (*DOHB-zheh, jen-KOO-yeh*)"],
  ["how do you say my name is in polish | my name is in polish | what is your name in polish", "In Polish, \"my name is …\" is **Mam na imię …** (*mahm nah EE-myeh*) — just add your name. Also **Nazywam się …**. To ask: **Jak masz na imię?**"],
  ["how do you say i love you in polish | i love you in polish | polish for i love you", "In Polish, \"I love you\" is **Kocham cię** (*KOH-hahm chyeh*)."],
  ["how do you say happy birthday in polish | happy birthday in polish | polish for happy birthday", "In Polish, \"happy birthday\" is **Wszystkiego najlepszego!** (*fshist-KYEH-goh nai-lep-SHEH-goh*). Literally \"all the best\". The birthday song is **Sto lat!** (a hundred years!)."],
  ["how do you say sorry in polish | how do you say excuse me in polish | sorry in polish | excuse me in polish", "In Polish, **Przepraszam** (*psheh-PRAH-shahm*) means both \"excuse me\" and \"sorry\"."],
  ["how do you say where is the bathroom in polish | where is the bathroom in polish | where is the toilet in polish", "In Polish, \"where is the bathroom?\" is **Gdzie jest toaleta?** (*gjeh yest toh-ah-LEH-tah*)."],
  ["how do you say i don't understand in polish | i don't understand in polish | i dont understand in polish", "In Polish, \"I don't understand\" is **Nie rozumiem** (*nyeh roh-ZOO-myem*)."],
  ["how do you say do you speak english in polish | do you speak english in polish | how to ask if someone speaks english in polish", "In Polish, \"do you speak English?\" is **Czy mówi pan po angielsku?** (*chi MOO-vee pahn poh ahn-GYEL-skoo*). Say **pan** to a man and **pani** to a woman. Casual: **Mówisz po angielsku?**"],
  ["how do you say how much is this in polish | how much is this in polish | how much does it cost in polish", "In Polish, \"how much is this?\" is **Ile to kosztuje?** (*EE-leh toh kosh-TOO-yeh*)."],
  ["how do you say nice to meet you in polish | nice to meet you in polish | polish for nice to meet you", "In Polish, \"nice to meet you\" is **Miło mi** (*MEE-woh mee*). Longer: **Miło cię poznać.**"],
  ["how do you say see you later in polish | see you later in polish | polish for see you later", "In Polish, \"see you later\" is **Do zobaczenia** (*doh zoh-bah-CHEH-nyah*). Literally \"until we see each other\". Casual: **Na razie!**"],
  ["count to ten in polish | how do you count to 10 in polish | numbers 1 to 10 in polish", "Counting to ten in Polish:\n1 — **jeden**\n2 — **dwa**\n3 — **trzy**\n4 — **cztery**\n5 — **pięć**\n6 — **sześć**\n7 — **siedem**\n8 — **osiem**\n9 — **dziewięć**\n10 — **dziesięć**"],
  ["days of the week in polish | how do you say monday in polish | polish days of the week", "The days of the week in Polish:\n• Monday — **poniedziałek**\n• Tuesday — **wtorek**\n• Wednesday — **środa**\n• Thursday — **czwartek**\n• Friday — **piątek**\n• Saturday — **sobota**\n• Sunday — **niedziela**\n*Niedziela* (Sunday) comes from \"not working\"."],
  ["colors in polish | colours in polish | how do you say red in polish", "Colors in Polish:\n• Red — **czerwony**\n• Orange — **pomarańczowy**\n• Yellow — **żółty**\n• Green — **zielony**\n• Blue — **niebieski**\n• Purple — **fioletowy**\n• Black — **czarny**\n• White — **biały**"],
  ["how do you say good morning in czech | good morning in czech | czech for good morning", "In Czech, good morning is **Dobré ráno** (*DOH-breh RAH-noh*). Later in the day, say **dobrý den** (good day)."],
  ["how do you say good night in czech | good night in czech | goodnight in czech", "In Czech, good night is **Dobrou noc** (*DOH-broh nots*)."],
  ["how do you say how are you in czech | how are you in czech | czech for how are you", "In Czech, \"how are you?\" is **Jak se máš?** (*yahk seh MAHSH*). Polite: **Jak se máte?**"],
  ["how do you say my name is in czech | my name is in czech | what is your name in czech", "In Czech, \"my name is …\" is **Jmenuji se …** (*YMEH-noo-yi seh*) — just add your name. To ask: **Jak se jmenuješ?**"],
  ["how do you say i love you in czech | i love you in czech | czech for i love you", "In Czech, \"I love you\" is **Miluji tě** (*MI-loo-yi tyeh*). In everyday speech: **Miluju tě.**"],
  ["how do you say happy birthday in czech | happy birthday in czech | czech for happy birthday", "In Czech, \"happy birthday\" is **Všechno nejlepší k narozeninám!** (*FSHEKH-noh NAY-lep-shee k NAH-roh-zeh-nee-nahm*)."],
  ["how do you say sorry in czech | how do you say excuse me in czech | sorry in czech | excuse me in czech", "In Czech, \"excuse me\" is **Promiňte** (*PROH-min-teh*) and \"sorry\" is **Omlouvám se** (*OHM-loh-vahm seh*). With friends, a quick **promiň** works for both."],
  ["how do you say where is the bathroom in czech | where is the bathroom in czech | where is the toilet in czech", "In Czech, \"where is the bathroom?\" is **Kde je toaleta?** (*gdeh yeh TOH-ah-leh-tah*)."],
  ["how do you say i don't understand in czech | i don't understand in czech | i dont understand in czech", "In Czech, \"I don't understand\" is **Nerozumím** (*NEH-roh-zoo-meem*)."],
  ["how do you say do you speak english in czech | do you speak english in czech | how to ask if someone speaks english in czech", "In Czech, \"do you speak English?\" is **Mluvíte anglicky?** (*MLOO-vee-teh AHN-glits-kee*)."],
  ["how do you say how much is this in czech | how much is this in czech | how much does it cost in czech", "In Czech, \"how much is this?\" is **Kolik to stojí?** (*KOH-lik toh STOH-yee*)."],
  ["how do you say nice to meet you in czech | nice to meet you in czech | czech for nice to meet you", "In Czech, \"nice to meet you\" is **Těší mě** (*TYEH-shee mnyeh*)."],
  ["how do you say see you later in czech | see you later in czech | czech for see you later", "In Czech, \"see you later\" is **Uvidíme se později** (*OO-vi-dee-meh seh POZ-dyeh-yi*). Casual: **Zatím!** (bye for now)."],
  ["count to ten in czech | how do you count to 10 in czech | numbers 1 to 10 in czech", "Counting to ten in Czech:\n1 — **jedna**\n2 — **dva**\n3 — **tři**\n4 — **čtyři**\n5 — **pět**\n6 — **šest**\n7 — **sedm**\n8 — **osm**\n9 — **devět**\n10 — **deset**\nWatch out for **ř** in *tři* — it's a famous Czech sound, like a rolled r and \"zh\" at the same time."],
  ["days of the week in czech | how do you say monday in czech | czech days of the week", "The days of the week in Czech:\n• Monday — **pondělí**\n• Tuesday — **úterý**\n• Wednesday — **středa**\n• Thursday — **čtvrtek**\n• Friday — **pátek**\n• Saturday — **sobota**\n• Sunday — **neděle**"],
  ["colors in czech | colours in czech | how do you say red in czech", "Colors in Czech:\n• Red — **červený**\n• Orange — **oranžový**\n• Yellow — **žlutý**\n• Green — **zelený**\n• Blue — **modrý**\n• Purple — **fialový**\n• Black — **černý**\n• White — **bílý**"],
  ["how do you say good morning in turkish | good morning in turkish | turkish for good morning", "In Turkish, good morning is **Günaydın** (*gew-nai-DUN*)."],
  ["how do you say good night in turkish | good night in turkish | goodnight in turkish", "In Turkish, good night is **İyi geceler** (*ee-YEE geh-jeh-LEHR*)."],
  ["how do you say how are you in turkish | how are you in turkish | turkish for how are you", "In Turkish, \"how are you?\" is **Nasılsın?** (*NAH-sul-sun*). Polite: **Nasılsınız?** Reply: **İyiyim, teşekkürler.**"],
  ["how do you say my name is in turkish | my name is in turkish | what is your name in turkish", "In Turkish, \"my name is …\" is **Benim adım …** (*beh-NEEM ah-DUHM*) — just add your name. To ask: **Adın ne?** (*ah-DUHN neh*)"],
  ["how do you say i love you in turkish | i love you in turkish | turkish for i love you", "In Turkish, \"I love you\" is **Seni seviyorum** (*seh-NEE seh-vee-YOH-room*)."],
  ["how do you say happy birthday in turkish | happy birthday in turkish | turkish for happy birthday", "In Turkish, \"happy birthday\" is **İyi ki doğdun!** (*ee-YEE kee doh-DOON*). Literally \"good thing you were born!\" Also **Doğum günün kutlu olsun!**"],
  ["how do you say sorry in turkish | how do you say excuse me in turkish | sorry in turkish | excuse me in turkish", "In Turkish, \"excuse me\" is **Affedersiniz** (*ahf-feh-DEHR-see-neez*) and \"sorry\" is **Özür dilerim** (*ur-ZEWR dee-leh-reem*)."],
  ["how do you say where is the bathroom in turkish | where is the bathroom in turkish | where is the toilet in turkish", "In Turkish, \"where is the bathroom?\" is **Tuvalet nerede?** (*too-vah-LET NEH-reh-deh*)."],
  ["how do you say i don't understand in turkish | i don't understand in turkish | i dont understand in turkish", "In Turkish, \"I don't understand\" is **Anlamıyorum** (*ahn-LAH-muh-yoh-room*)."],
  ["how do you say do you speak english in turkish | do you speak english in turkish | how to ask if someone speaks english in turkish", "In Turkish, \"do you speak English?\" is **İngilizce biliyor musunuz?** (*een-gee-LEEZ-jeh bee-lee-YOR moo-soo-nooz*)."],
  ["how do you say how much is this in turkish | how much is this in turkish | how much does it cost in turkish", "In Turkish, \"how much is this?\" is **Bu ne kadar?** (*boo NEH kah-dar*)."],
  ["how do you say nice to meet you in turkish | nice to meet you in turkish | turkish for nice to meet you", "In Turkish, \"nice to meet you\" is **Memnun oldum** (*mem-NOON ol-DOOM*)."],
  ["how do you say see you later in turkish | see you later in turkish | turkish for see you later", "In Turkish, \"see you later\" is **Sonra görüşürüz** (*SON-rah gur-rew-shew-REWZ*). Short: **Görüşürüz!**"],
  ["count to ten in turkish | how do you count to 10 in turkish | numbers 1 to 10 in turkish", "Counting to ten in Turkish:\n1 — **bir**\n2 — **iki**\n3 — **üç**\n4 — **dört**\n5 — **beş**\n6 — **altı**\n7 — **yedi**\n8 — **sekiz**\n9 — **dokuz**\n10 — **on**"],
  ["days of the week in turkish | how do you say monday in turkish | turkish days of the week", "The days of the week in Turkish:\n• Monday — **Pazartesi**\n• Tuesday — **Salı**\n• Wednesday — **Çarşamba**\n• Thursday — **Perşembe**\n• Friday — **Cuma**\n• Saturday — **Cumartesi**\n• Sunday — **Pazar**\n*Pazartesi* (Monday) means \"after market day\", because *Pazar* (Sunday) was market day."],
  ["colors in turkish | colours in turkish | how do you say red in turkish", "Colors in Turkish:\n• Red — **kırmızı**\n• Orange — **turuncu**\n• Yellow — **sarı**\n• Green — **yeşil**\n• Blue — **mavi**\n• Purple — **mor**\n• Black — **siyah**\n• White — **beyaz**"],
  ["how do you say good morning in vietnamese | good morning in vietnamese | vietnamese for good morning", "In Vietnamese, good morning is **Chào buổi sáng** (*chow bwee SAHNG*). Day to day, most people just say **Xin chào** or **Chào** + a title, like *Chào bạn*."],
  ["how do you say good night in vietnamese | good night in vietnamese | goodnight in vietnamese", "In Vietnamese, good night is **Chúc ngủ ngon** (*chook ngoo NGON*)."],
  ["how do you say how are you in vietnamese | how are you in vietnamese | vietnamese for how are you", "In Vietnamese, \"how are you?\" is **Bạn có khỏe không?** (*bahn kaw KWEH khohng*). Reply: **Tôi khỏe, cảm ơn!** (I'm well, thanks!)"],
  ["how do you say my name is in vietnamese | my name is in vietnamese | what is your name in vietnamese", "In Vietnamese, \"my name is …\" is **Tôi tên là …** (*toy ten LAH*) — just add your name. To ask: **Bạn tên là gì?** (*bahn ten lah ZEE*)"],
  ["how do you say i love you in vietnamese | i love you in vietnamese | vietnamese for i love you", "In Vietnamese, \"I love you\" is **Tôi yêu bạn** (*toy EE-oo bahn*). Vietnamese changes the word for \"I\" and \"you\" by relationship — a child tells Mom **Con yêu mẹ** (*kon EE-oo meh*)."],
  ["how do you say happy birthday in vietnamese | happy birthday in vietnamese | vietnamese for happy birthday", "In Vietnamese, \"happy birthday\" is **Chúc mừng sinh nhật!** (*chook MUNG sin NYUT*)."],
  ["how do you say sorry in vietnamese | how do you say excuse me in vietnamese | sorry in vietnamese | excuse me in vietnamese", "In Vietnamese, **Xin lỗi** (*sin LOY*) means both \"excuse me\" and \"sorry\"."],
  ["how do you say where is the bathroom in vietnamese | where is the bathroom in vietnamese | where is the toilet in vietnamese", "In Vietnamese, \"where is the bathroom?\" is **Nhà vệ sinh ở đâu?** (*nyah veh SIN uh DOH*)."],
  ["how do you say i don't understand in vietnamese | i don't understand in vietnamese | i dont understand in vietnamese", "In Vietnamese, \"I don't understand\" is **Tôi không hiểu** (*toy khohng HIEW*)."],
  ["how do you say do you speak english in vietnamese | do you speak english in vietnamese | how to ask if someone speaks english in vietnamese", "In Vietnamese, \"do you speak English?\" is **Bạn có nói tiếng Anh không?** (*bahn kaw NOY tee-ung AHN khohng*)."],
  ["how do you say how much is this in vietnamese | how much is this in vietnamese | how much does it cost in vietnamese", "In Vietnamese, \"how much is this?\" is **Cái này bao nhiêu tiền?** (*kai nai bow NYEW tee-en*)."],
  ["how do you say nice to meet you in vietnamese | nice to meet you in vietnamese | vietnamese for nice to meet you", "In Vietnamese, \"nice to meet you\" is **Rất vui được gặp bạn** (*zut VOO-ee duh-uk gup bahn*)."],
  ["how do you say see you later in vietnamese | see you later in vietnamese | vietnamese for see you later", "In Vietnamese, \"see you later\" is **Hẹn gặp lại** (*hen gup LAI*). Literally \"promise to meet again\"."],
  ["count to ten in vietnamese | how do you count to 10 in vietnamese | numbers 1 to 10 in vietnamese", "Counting to ten in Vietnamese:\n1 — **một**\n2 — **hai**\n3 — **ba**\n4 — **bốn**\n5 — **năm**\n6 — **sáu**\n7 — **bảy**\n8 — **tám**\n9 — **chín**\n10 — **mười**\nVietnamese has six tones, so the accent marks really matter!"],
  ["days of the week in vietnamese | how do you say monday in vietnamese | vietnamese days of the week", "The days of the week in Vietnamese:\n• Monday — **Thứ Hai**\n• Tuesday — **Thứ Ba**\n• Wednesday — **Thứ Tư**\n• Thursday — **Thứ Năm**\n• Friday — **Thứ Sáu**\n• Saturday — **Thứ Bảy**\n• Sunday — **Chủ Nhật**\nMonday is literally \"second day\", Tuesday \"third day\", and so on. *Chủ Nhật* (Sunday) means \"Lord's day\"."],
  ["colors in vietnamese | colours in vietnamese | how do you say red in vietnamese", "Colors in Vietnamese:\n• Red — **đỏ**\n• Orange — **cam**\n• Yellow — **vàng**\n• Green — **xanh lá cây**\n• Blue — **xanh dương**\n• Purple — **tím**\n• Black — **đen**\n• White — **trắng**\n*Xanh* can mean blue or green, so people add *lá cây* (leaf) or *dương* (ocean) to be clear."],
  ["how do you say good morning in indonesian | good morning in indonesian | indonesian for good morning | good morning in bahasa indonesia", "In Indonesian, good morning is **Selamat pagi** (*seh-LAH-maht PAH-gee*)."],
  ["how do you say good night in indonesian | good night in indonesian | goodnight in indonesian | good night in bahasa indonesia", "In Indonesian, good night is **Selamat tidur** (*seh-LAH-maht TEE-door*). Literally \"happy sleeping\". **Selamat malam** means good evening."],
  ["how do you say how are you in indonesian | how are you in indonesian | indonesian for how are you | how are you in bahasa indonesia", "In Indonesian, \"how are you?\" is **Apa kabar?** (*AH-pah KAH-bar*). Reply: **Baik, terima kasih!** (*BAH-eek, teh-REE-mah KAH-see*)"],
  ["how do you say my name is in indonesian | my name is in indonesian | what is your name in indonesian | how do you say my name is in bahasa indonesia", "In Indonesian, \"my name is …\" is **Nama saya …** (*NAH-mah SAH-yah*) — just add your name. To ask: **Siapa nama Anda?** (*see-AH-pah NAH-mah AHN-dah*)"],
  ["how do you say i love you in indonesian | i love you in indonesian | indonesian for i love you | i love you in bahasa indonesia", "In Indonesian, \"I love you\" is **Aku sayang kamu** (*AH-koo SAH-yahng KAH-moo*). This is the warm way to say it to family and friends. Romantic love is **Aku cinta kamu**."],
  ["how do you say happy birthday in indonesian | happy birthday in indonesian | indonesian for happy birthday | happy birthday in bahasa indonesia", "In Indonesian, \"happy birthday\" is **Selamat ulang tahun!** (*seh-LAH-maht OO-lahng TAH-hoon*)."],
  ["how do you say sorry in indonesian | how do you say excuse me in indonesian | sorry in indonesian | excuse me in indonesian", "In Indonesian, \"excuse me\" is **Permisi** (*per-MEE-see*) and \"sorry\" is **Maaf** (*MAH-ahf*)."],
  ["how do you say where is the bathroom in indonesian | where is the bathroom in indonesian | where is the toilet in indonesian | where is the bathroom in bahasa indonesia", "In Indonesian, \"where is the bathroom?\" is **Di mana kamar mandi?** (*dee MAH-nah KAH-mar MAHN-dee*). Many people also just say **toilet**."],
  ["how do you say i don't understand in indonesian | i don't understand in indonesian | i dont understand in indonesian | i don't understand in bahasa indonesia", "In Indonesian, \"I don't understand\" is **Saya tidak mengerti** (*SAH-yah TEE-dahk meng-ER-tee*)."],
  ["how do you say do you speak english in indonesian | do you speak english in indonesian | how to ask if someone speaks english in indonesian | do you speak english in bahasa indonesia", "In Indonesian, \"do you speak English?\" is **Apakah Anda bisa berbahasa Inggris?** (*ah-PAH-kah AHN-dah BEE-sah ber-bah-HAH-sah ING-grees*). Simpler: **Bisa bahasa Inggris?**"],
  ["how do you say how much is this in indonesian | how much is this in indonesian | how much does it cost in indonesian | how much is this in bahasa indonesia", "In Indonesian, \"how much is this?\" is **Berapa harganya?** (*beh-RAH-pah har-GAH-nyah*)."],
  ["how do you say nice to meet you in indonesian | nice to meet you in indonesian | indonesian for nice to meet you | nice to meet you in bahasa indonesia", "In Indonesian, \"nice to meet you\" is **Senang bertemu dengan Anda** (*seh-NAHNG ber-TEH-moo deh-NGAHN AHN-dah*)."],
  ["how do you say see you later in indonesian | see you later in indonesian | indonesian for see you later | see you later in bahasa indonesia", "In Indonesian, \"see you later\" is **Sampai nanti** (*SAHM-pai NAHN-tee*). Also **Sampai jumpa!** (see you!)."],
  ["count to ten in indonesian | how do you count to 10 in indonesian | numbers 1 to 10 in indonesian | count to ten in bahasa indonesia", "Counting to ten in Indonesian:\n1 — **satu**\n2 — **dua**\n3 — **tiga**\n4 — **empat**\n5 — **lima**\n6 — **enam**\n7 — **tujuh**\n8 — **delapan**\n9 — **sembilan**\n10 — **sepuluh**"],
  ["days of the week in indonesian | how do you say monday in indonesian | indonesian days of the week | days of the week in bahasa indonesia", "The days of the week in Indonesian:\n• Monday — **Senin**\n• Tuesday — **Selasa**\n• Wednesday — **Rabu**\n• Thursday — **Kamis**\n• Friday — **Jumat**\n• Saturday — **Sabtu**\n• Sunday — **Minggu**"],
  ["colors in indonesian | colours in indonesian | how do you say red in indonesian | colors in bahasa indonesia", "Colors in Indonesian:\n• Red — **merah**\n• Orange — **oranye**\n• Yellow — **kuning**\n• Green — **hijau**\n• Blue — **biru**\n• Purple — **ungu**\n• Black — **hitam**\n• White — **putih**\nRed and white (*merah putih*) are the colors of Indonesia's flag."],
  ["how do you say good morning in tagalog | good morning in tagalog | tagalog for good morning | good morning in filipino", "In Tagalog (Filipino), good morning is **Magandang umaga** (*mah-gahn-DAHNG oo-MAH-gah*). Add **po** to be polite to elders: *Magandang umaga po.*"],
  ["how do you say good night in tagalog | good night in tagalog | goodnight in tagalog | good night in filipino", "In Tagalog (Filipino), good night is **Magandang gabi** (*mah-gahn-DAHNG gah-BEE*). It means both good evening and good night. Many Filipinos also simply say \"good night\" in English."],
  ["how do you say how are you in tagalog | how are you in tagalog | tagalog for how are you | how are you in filipino", "In Tagalog (Filipino), \"how are you?\" is **Kumusta ka?** (*koo-MOOS-tah kah*). Polite: **Kumusta po kayo?** Reply: **Mabuti, salamat!** (*mah-BOO-tee, sah-LAH-maht*)"],
  ["how do you say my name is in tagalog | my name is in tagalog | what is your name in tagalog | how do you say my name is in filipino", "In Tagalog (Filipino), \"my name is …\" is **Ako si …** (*ah-KOH see*) — just add your name. Also **Ang pangalan ko ay …**. To ask: **Ano ang pangalan mo?**"],
  ["how do you say i love you in tagalog | i love you in tagalog | tagalog for i love you | i love you in filipino", "In Tagalog (Filipino), \"I love you\" is **Mahal kita** (*mah-HAHL KEE-tah*). Said to family, friends and sweethearts alike."],
  ["how do you say happy birthday in tagalog | happy birthday in tagalog | tagalog for happy birthday | happy birthday in filipino", "In Tagalog (Filipino), \"happy birthday\" is **Maligayang kaarawan!** (*mah-lee-GAH-yahng kah-ah-RAH-wahn*)."],
  ["how do you say sorry in tagalog | how do you say excuse me in tagalog | sorry in tagalog | excuse me in tagalog", "In Tagalog (Filipino), \"excuse me\" is **Paumanhin po** (*pah-oo-MAHN-hin poh*) and \"sorry\" is **Pasensya na** (*pah-SEN-shah nah*). To squeeze past people, say **Makikiraan po**."],
  ["how do you say where is the bathroom in tagalog | where is the bathroom in tagalog | where is the toilet in tagalog | where is the bathroom in filipino", "In Tagalog (Filipino), \"where is the bathroom?\" is **Nasaan ang banyo?** (*nah-SAH-ahn ahng BAHN-yoh*). In the Philippines the bathroom is also called the **CR** (\"comfort room\")!"],
  ["how do you say i don't understand in tagalog | i don't understand in tagalog | i dont understand in tagalog | i don't understand in filipino", "In Tagalog (Filipino), \"I don't understand\" is **Hindi ko maintindihan** (*hin-DEE koh mah-in-tin-dee-HAHN*)."],
  ["how do you say do you speak english in tagalog | do you speak english in tagalog | how to ask if someone speaks english in tagalog | do you speak english in filipino", "In Tagalog (Filipino), \"do you speak English?\" is **Marunong ka bang mag-Ingles?** (*mah-ROO-nong kah bahng mahg-ING-gles*). Lots of Filipinos speak English very well."],
  ["how do you say how much is this in tagalog | how much is this in tagalog | how much does it cost in tagalog | how much is this in filipino", "In Tagalog (Filipino), \"how much is this?\" is **Magkano ito?** (*mahg-KAH-noh EE-toh*)."],
  ["how do you say nice to meet you in tagalog | nice to meet you in tagalog | tagalog for nice to meet you | nice to meet you in filipino", "In Tagalog (Filipino), \"nice to meet you\" is **Ikinagagalak kong makilala ka** (*ee-kee-nah-gah-GAH-lahk kong mah-kee-LAH-lah kah*)."],
  ["how do you say see you later in tagalog | see you later in tagalog | tagalog for see you later | see you later in filipino", "In Tagalog (Filipino), \"see you later\" is **Kita tayo mamaya** (*KEE-tah TAH-yoh mah-MAH-yah*). Casual: **Kitakits!**"],
  ["count to ten in tagalog | how do you count to 10 in tagalog | numbers 1 to 10 in tagalog | count to ten in filipino", "Counting to ten in Tagalog (Filipino):\n1 — **isa**\n2 — **dalawa**\n3 — **tatlo**\n4 — **apat**\n5 — **lima**\n6 — **anim**\n7 — **pito**\n8 — **walo**\n9 — **siyam**\n10 — **sampu**\nFor prices and time, Filipinos often use Spanish-based numbers like *uno, dos, tres*."],
  ["days of the week in tagalog | how do you say monday in tagalog | tagalog days of the week | days of the week in filipino", "The days of the week in Tagalog (Filipino):\n• Monday — **Lunes**\n• Tuesday — **Martes**\n• Wednesday — **Miyerkules**\n• Thursday — **Huwebes**\n• Friday — **Biyernes**\n• Saturday — **Sabado**\n• Sunday — **Linggo**\nMost of the day names come from Spanish."],
  ["colors in tagalog | colours in tagalog | how do you say red in tagalog | colors in filipino", "Colors in Tagalog (Filipino):\n• Red — **pula**\n• Orange — **kahel**\n• Yellow — **dilaw**\n• Green — **berde**\n• Blue — **asul**\n• Purple — **lila**\n• Black — **itim**\n• White — **puti**"],
  ["how do you say good morning in swahili | good morning in swahili | swahili for good morning | good morning in kiswahili", "In Swahili, good morning is **Habari za asubuhi** (*hah-BAH-ree zah ah-soo-BOO-hee*). Literally \"news of the morning?\" Reply: **Nzuri** (*n-ZOO-ree*, good)."],
  ["how do you say good night in swahili | good night in swahili | goodnight in swahili | good night in kiswahili", "In Swahili, good night is **Usiku mwema** (*oo-SEE-koo MWEH-mah*). Also **Lala salama** (*LAH-lah sah-LAH-mah*, sleep well)."],
  ["how do you say how are you in swahili | how are you in swahili | swahili for how are you | how are you in kiswahili", "In Swahili, \"how are you?\" is **Habari yako?** (*hah-BAH-ree YAH-koh*). Reply: **Nzuri!** Another classic: **Hujambo?** (*hoo-JAHM-boh*), answered with **Sijambo** (I'm fine)."],
  ["how do you say my name is in swahili | my name is in swahili | what is your name in swahili | how do you say my name is in kiswahili", "In Swahili, \"my name is …\" is **Jina langu ni …** (*JEE-nah LAHN-goo nee*) — just add your name. To ask: **Jina lako nani?** (*JEE-nah LAH-koh NAH-nee*)"],
  ["how do you say i love you in swahili | i love you in swahili | swahili for i love you | i love you in kiswahili", "In Swahili, \"I love you\" is **Nakupenda** (*nah-koo-PEN-dah*)."],
  ["how do you say happy birthday in swahili | happy birthday in swahili | swahili for happy birthday | happy birthday in kiswahili", "In Swahili, \"happy birthday\" is **Heri ya siku ya kuzaliwa!** (*HEH-ree yah SEE-koo yah koo-zah-LEE-wah*)."],
  ["how do you say sorry in swahili | how do you say excuse me in swahili | sorry in swahili | excuse me in swahili", "In Swahili, **Samahani** (*sah-mah-HAH-nee*) means both \"excuse me\" and \"sorry\". To show sympathy when something bad happens to someone, say **Pole** (*POH-leh*)."],
  ["how do you say where is the bathroom in swahili | where is the bathroom in swahili | where is the toilet in swahili | where is the bathroom in kiswahili", "In Swahili, \"where is the bathroom?\" is **Choo kiko wapi?** (*CHOH-oh KEE-koh WAH-pee*)."],
  ["how do you say i don't understand in swahili | i don't understand in swahili | i dont understand in swahili | i don't understand in kiswahili", "In Swahili, \"I don't understand\" is **Sielewi** (*see-eh-LEH-wee*)."],
  ["how do you say do you speak english in swahili | do you speak english in swahili | how to ask if someone speaks english in swahili | do you speak english in kiswahili", "In Swahili, \"do you speak English?\" is **Unaongea Kiingereza?** (*oo-nah-ohn-GEH-ah kee-een-geh-REH-zah*). Also: **Unazungumza Kiingereza?**"],
  ["how do you say how much is this in swahili | how much is this in swahili | how much does it cost in swahili | how much is this in kiswahili", "In Swahili, \"how much is this?\" is **Hii ni bei gani?** (*HEE-ee nee BAY GAH-nee*). Shorter: **Bei gani?**"],
  ["how do you say nice to meet you in swahili | nice to meet you in swahili | swahili for nice to meet you | nice to meet you in kiswahili", "In Swahili, \"nice to meet you\" is **Nimefurahi kukutana nawe** (*nee-meh-foo-RAH-hee koo-koo-TAH-nah NAH-weh*)."],
  ["how do you say see you later in swahili | see you later in swahili | swahili for see you later | see you later in kiswahili", "In Swahili, \"see you later\" is **Tutaonana baadaye** (*too-tah-oh-NAH-nah bah-ah-DAH-yeh*)."],
  ["count to ten in swahili | how do you count to 10 in swahili | numbers 1 to 10 in swahili | count to ten in kiswahili", "Counting to ten in Swahili:\n1 — **moja**\n2 — **mbili**\n3 — **tatu**\n4 — **nne**\n5 — **tano**\n6 — **sita**\n7 — **saba**\n8 — **nane**\n9 — **tisa**\n10 — **kumi**"],
  ["days of the week in swahili | how do you say monday in swahili | swahili days of the week | days of the week in kiswahili", "The days of the week in Swahili:\n• Monday — **Jumatatu**\n• Tuesday — **Jumanne**\n• Wednesday — **Jumatano**\n• Thursday — **Alhamisi**\n• Friday — **Ijumaa**\n• Saturday — **Jumamosi**\n• Sunday — **Jumapili**\nThe Swahili week counts from Saturday (*Jumamosi*, \"day one\"), so Monday, *Jumatatu*, is \"day three\"."],
  ["colors in swahili | colours in swahili | how do you say red in swahili | colors in kiswahili", "Colors in Swahili:\n• Red — **nyekundu**\n• Orange — **rangi ya chungwa**\n• Yellow — **njano**\n• Green — **kijani**\n• Blue — **bluu**\n• Purple — **zambarau**\n• Black — **nyeusi**\n• White — **nyeupe**\nOrange is *rangi ya chungwa* — literally \"the color of an orange\"."],
  ["how do you say good morning in irish | good morning in irish | irish for good morning | good morning in irish gaelic", "In Irish, good morning is **Dia duit ar maidin** (*DEE-ah gwit er MAH-jin*). Literally \"God be with you in the morning\". Also **Maidin mhaith** (*MAH-jin wah*)."],
  ["how do you say good night in irish | good night in irish | goodnight in irish | good night in irish gaelic", "In Irish, good night is **Oíche mhaith** (*EE-heh wah*)."],
  ["how do you say how are you in irish | how are you in irish | irish for how are you | how are you in irish gaelic", "In Irish, \"how are you?\" is **Conas atá tú?** (*KUN-us ah-TAW too*). That's the Munster way; in Connacht you'll hear **Cén chaoi a bhfuil tú?** Reply: **Tá mé go maith** (*taw may guh mah*, I'm well)."],
  ["how do you say my name is in irish | my name is in irish | what is your name in irish | how do you say my name is in irish gaelic", "In Irish, \"my name is …\" is **Is mise …** (*iss MISH-eh*) — just add your name. To ask: **Cad is ainm duit?** (*kod iss AN-im ditch*)"],
  ["how do you say i love you in irish | i love you in irish | irish for i love you | i love you in irish gaelic", "In Irish, \"I love you\" is **Is breá liom thú** (*iss BRAW lum hoo*). Also **Tá grá agam duit** (*taw graw AH-gum ditch*)."],
  ["how do you say happy birthday in irish | happy birthday in irish | irish for happy birthday | happy birthday in irish gaelic", "In Irish, \"happy birthday\" is **Lá breithe sona duit!** (*law BREH-heh SUN-ah ditch*)."],
  ["how do you say sorry in irish | how do you say excuse me in irish | sorry in irish | excuse me in irish", "In Irish, **Gabh mo leithscéal** (*gow muh LESH-kayl*) means both \"excuse me\" and \"sorry\". To say you feel sorry or sad about something: **Tá brón orm** (*taw brohn OR-um*)."],
  ["how do you say where is the bathroom in irish | where is the bathroom in irish | where is the toilet in irish | where is the bathroom in irish gaelic", "In Irish, \"where is the bathroom?\" is **Cá bhfuil an leithreas?** (*kaw will on LEH-ris*)."],
  ["how do you say i don't understand in irish | i don't understand in irish | i dont understand in irish | i don't understand in irish gaelic", "In Irish, \"I don't understand\" is **Ní thuigim** (*nee HIG-im*)."],
  ["how do you say do you speak english in irish | do you speak english in irish | how to ask if someone speaks english in irish | do you speak english in irish gaelic", "In Irish, \"do you speak English?\" is **An bhfuil Béarla agat?** (*on will BAYR-lah AH-gut*). Literally \"Do you have English?\""],
  ["how do you say how much is this in irish | how much is this in irish | how much does it cost in irish | how much is this in irish gaelic", "In Irish, \"how much is this?\" is **Cé mhéad atá air seo?** (*kay vayd ah-TAW er shuh*)."],
  ["how do you say nice to meet you in irish | nice to meet you in irish | irish for nice to meet you | nice to meet you in irish gaelic", "In Irish, \"nice to meet you\" is **Tá áthas orm bualadh leat** (*taw AW-hass OR-um BOO-lah lat*)."],
  ["how do you say see you later in irish | see you later in irish | irish for see you later | see you later in irish gaelic", "In Irish, \"see you later\" is **Feicfidh mé níos déanaí thú** (*FEK-ee may nee-us DAY-nee hoo*). Short: **Slán go fóill** (*slawn guh FOH-il*, bye for now)."],
  ["count to ten in irish | how do you count to 10 in irish | numbers 1 to 10 in irish | count to ten in irish gaelic", "Counting to ten in Irish:\n1 — **a haon** (*ah hayn*)\n2 — **a dó** (*ah doh*)\n3 — **a trí** (*ah tree*)\n4 — **a ceathair** (*ah KAH-her*)\n5 — **a cúig** (*ah KOO-ig*)\n6 — **a sé** (*ah shay*)\n7 — **a seacht** (*ah shokht*)\n8 — **a hocht** (*ah hokht*)\n9 — **a naoi** (*ah nee*)\n10 — **a deich** (*ah jeh*)"],
  ["days of the week in irish | how do you say monday in irish | irish days of the week | days of the week in irish gaelic", "The days of the week in Irish:\n• Monday — **Dé Luain**\n• Tuesday — **Dé Máirt**\n• Wednesday — **Dé Céadaoin**\n• Thursday — **Déardaoin**\n• Friday — **Dé hAoine**\n• Saturday — **Dé Sathairn**\n• Sunday — **Dé Domhnaigh**"],
  ["colors in irish | colours in irish | how do you say red in irish | colors in irish gaelic", "Colors in Irish:\n• Red — **dearg**\n• Orange — **oráiste**\n• Yellow — **buí**\n• Green — **glas**\n• Blue — **gorm**\n• Purple — **corcra**\n• Black — **dubh**\n• White — **bán**\n*Glas* is the green of grass and leaves; bright, artificial green is *uaine*."],
  ["how do you say good morning in greek | good morning in greek | greek for good morning", "In Greek, good morning is **Καλημέρα** (*kah-lee-MEH-rah*)."],
  ["how do you say good night in greek | good night in greek | goodnight in greek", "In Greek, good night is **Καληνύχτα** (*kah-lee-NEEKH-tah*). Good evening is **Καλησπέρα** (*kah-lee-SPEH-rah*)."],
  ["how do you say how are you in greek | how are you in greek | greek for how are you", "In Greek, \"how are you?\" is **Τι κάνεις;** (*tee KAH-nees*). Polite: **Τι κάνετε;** (*tee KAH-neh-teh*). Fun fact: Greek uses **;** as its question mark!"],
  ["how do you say my name is in greek | my name is in greek | what is your name in greek", "In Greek, \"my name is …\" is **Με λένε …** (*meh LEH-neh*) — just add your name. To ask: **Πώς σε λένε;** (*pos seh LEH-neh*)"],
  ["how do you say i love you in greek | i love you in greek | greek for i love you", "In Greek, \"I love you\" is **Σ' αγαπώ** (*sah-gah-POH*). Greeks say it to family as well as sweethearts."],
  ["how do you say happy birthday in greek | happy birthday in greek | greek for happy birthday", "In Greek, \"happy birthday\" is **Χρόνια πολλά!** (*KHROH-nyah poh-LAH*). Literally \"many years\" — used for birthdays, name days and holidays."],
  ["how do you say sorry in greek | how do you say excuse me in greek | sorry in greek | excuse me in greek", "In Greek, **Συγγνώμη** (*seeg-NOH-mee*) means both \"excuse me\" and \"sorry\"."],
  ["how do you say where is the bathroom in greek | where is the bathroom in greek | where is the toilet in greek", "In Greek, \"where is the bathroom?\" is **Πού είναι η τουαλέτα;** (*poo EE-neh ee too-ah-LEH-tah*)."],
  ["how do you say i don't understand in greek | i don't understand in greek | i dont understand in greek", "In Greek, \"I don't understand\" is **Δεν καταλαβαίνω** (*then kah-tah-lah-VEH-noh*). (The *th* sounds like the *th* in \"this\".)"],
  ["how do you say do you speak english in greek | do you speak english in greek | how to ask if someone speaks english in greek", "In Greek, \"do you speak English?\" is **Μιλάτε αγγλικά;** (*mee-LAH-teh ahn-glee-KAH*)."],
  ["how do you say how much is this in greek | how much is this in greek | how much does it cost in greek", "In Greek, \"how much is this?\" is **Πόσο κάνει;** (*POH-soh KAH-nee*)."],
  ["how do you say nice to meet you in greek | nice to meet you in greek | greek for nice to meet you", "In Greek, \"nice to meet you\" is **Χάρηκα** (*KHAH-ree-kah*). Also **Χαίρω πολύ** (*KHEH-roh poh-LEE*)."],
  ["how do you say see you later in greek | see you later in greek | greek for see you later", "In Greek, \"see you later\" is **Τα λέμε αργότερα** (*tah LEH-meh ar-GOH-teh-rah*). Short: **Τα λέμε!** (Talk soon!)"],
  ["count to ten in greek | how do you count to 10 in greek | numbers 1 to 10 in greek", "Counting to ten in Greek:\n1 — **ένα** (*EH-nah*)\n2 — **δύο** (*THEE-oh*)\n3 — **τρία** (*TREE-ah*)\n4 — **τέσσερα** (*TEH-seh-rah*)\n5 — **πέντε** (*PEN-deh*)\n6 — **έξι** (*EK-see*)\n7 — **επτά** (*ep-TAH*)\n8 — **οκτώ** (*ohk-TOH*)\n9 — **εννέα** (*eh-NEH-ah*)\n10 — **δέκα** (*THEH-kah*)"],
  ["days of the week in greek | how do you say monday in greek | greek days of the week", "The days of the week in Greek:\n• Monday — **Δευτέρα** (*thef-TEH-rah*)\n• Tuesday — **Τρίτη** (*TREE-tee*)\n• Wednesday — **Τετάρτη** (*teh-TAR-tee*)\n• Thursday — **Πέμπτη** (*PEMP-tee*)\n• Friday — **Παρασκευή** (*pah-rah-skeh-VEE*)\n• Saturday — **Σάββατο** (*SAH-vah-toh*)\n• Sunday — **Κυριακή** (*kee-ree-ah-KEE*)\nMonday to Thursday are just numbers: \"second\", \"third\", \"fourth\" and \"fifth\" day."],
  ["colors in greek | colours in greek | how do you say red in greek", "Colors in Greek:\n• Red — **κόκκινο** (*KOH-kee-noh*)\n• Orange — **πορτοκαλί** (*por-toh-kah-LEE*)\n• Yellow — **κίτρινο** (*KEE-tree-noh*)\n• Green — **πράσινο** (*PRAH-see-noh*)\n• Blue — **μπλε** (*bleh*)\n• Purple — **μωβ** (*mohv*)\n• Black — **μαύρο** (*MAHV-roh*)\n• White — **άσπρο** (*AHS-proh*)\n*Πορτοκαλί* (orange) comes from *πορτοκάλι*, the fruit."],
  ["how do you say good morning in russian | good morning in russian | russian for good morning", "In Russian, good morning is **Доброе утро** (*DOH-bruh-yeh OO-truh*)."],
  ["how do you say good night in russian | good night in russian | goodnight in russian", "In Russian, good night is **Спокойной ночи** (*spah-KOY-noy NOH-chee*). Good evening is **Добрый вечер** (*DOH-bry VYEH-cher*)."],
  ["how do you say how are you in russian | how are you in russian | russian for how are you", "In Russian, \"how are you?\" is **Как дела?** (*kahk dee-LAH*). Polite: **Как вы поживаете?** (*kahk vy pah-zhee-VAH-ee-tyeh*). Reply: **Хорошо, спасибо!** (*khah-rah-SHOH, spah-SEE-bah*)"],
  ["how do you say my name is in russian | my name is in russian | what is your name in russian", "In Russian, \"my name is …\" is **Меня зовут …** (*mee-NYA zah-VOOT*) — just add your name. To ask: **Как тебя зовут?** (*kahk tee-BYA zah-VOOT*)"],
  ["how do you say i love you in russian | i love you in russian | russian for i love you", "In Russian, \"I love you\" is **Я тебя люблю** (*ya tee-BYA lyoo-BLYOO*). Said to family as well as sweethearts."],
  ["how do you say happy birthday in russian | happy birthday in russian | russian for happy birthday", "In Russian, \"happy birthday\" is **С днём рождения!** (*s DNYOM rahzh-DYEH-nee-ya*)."],
  ["how do you say sorry in russian | how do you say excuse me in russian | sorry in russian | excuse me in russian", "In Russian, **Извините** (*eez-vee-NEE-tyeh*) means both \"excuse me\" and \"sorry\". With friends, a quick sorry is **Прости** (*prah-STEE*)."],
  ["how do you say where is the bathroom in russian | where is the bathroom in russian | where is the toilet in russian", "In Russian, \"where is the bathroom?\" is **Где туалет?** (*gdyeh too-ah-LYET*)."],
  ["how do you say i don't understand in russian | i don't understand in russian | i dont understand in russian", "In Russian, \"I don't understand\" is **Я не понимаю** (*ya nee pah-nee-MAH-yu*)."],
  ["how do you say do you speak english in russian | do you speak english in russian | how to ask if someone speaks english in russian", "In Russian, \"do you speak English?\" is **Вы говорите по-английски?** (*vy gah-vah-REE-tyeh pah-ahn-GLEE-skee*)."],
  ["how do you say how much is this in russian | how much is this in russian | how much does it cost in russian", "In Russian, \"how much is this?\" is **Сколько это стоит?** (*SKOL-kah EH-tah STOH-eet*)."],
  ["how do you say nice to meet you in russian | nice to meet you in russian | russian for nice to meet you", "In Russian, \"nice to meet you\" is **Очень приятно** (*OH-chen pree-YAHT-nah*)."],
  ["how do you say see you later in russian | see you later in russian | russian for see you later", "In Russian, \"see you later\" is **Увидимся позже** (*oo-VEE-deem-sya POZH-zheh*). Also **До встречи!** (*dah FSTREH-chee*, see you!) and **Пока!** (*pah-KAH*, bye!)."],
  ["count to ten in russian | how do you count to 10 in russian | numbers 1 to 10 in russian", "Counting to ten in Russian:\n1 — **один** (*ah-DEEN*)\n2 — **два** (*dvah*)\n3 — **три** (*tree*)\n4 — **четыре** (*chee-TY-ree*)\n5 — **пять** (*pyat*)\n6 — **шесть** (*shest*)\n7 — **семь** (*syem*)\n8 — **восемь** (*VOH-seem*)\n9 — **девять** (*DYEH-veet*)\n10 — **десять** (*DYEH-seet*)"],
  ["days of the week in russian | how do you say monday in russian | russian days of the week", "The days of the week in Russian:\n• Monday — **понедельник** (*pah-nee-DYEL-neek*)\n• Tuesday — **вторник** (*FTOR-neek*)\n• Wednesday — **среда** (*sree-DAH*)\n• Thursday — **четверг** (*cheet-VYERK*)\n• Friday — **пятница** (*PYAT-nee-tsah*)\n• Saturday — **суббота** (*soo-BOH-tah*)\n• Sunday — **воскресенье** (*vahs-kree-SYEN-yeh*)\nRussian doesn't capitalize the days. *Вторник* (Tuesday) comes from the word for \"second\"."],
  ["colors in russian | colours in russian | how do you say red in russian", "Colors in Russian:\n• Red — **красный** (*KRAHS-ny*)\n• Orange — **оранжевый** (*ah-RAHN-zheh-vy*)\n• Yellow — **жёлтый** (*ZHOL-ty*)\n• Green — **зелёный** (*zee-LYO-ny*)\n• Blue — **синий** (*SEE-nee*)\n• Purple — **фиолетовый** (*fee-ah-LYEH-tah-vy*)\n• Black — **чёрный** (*CHOR-ny*)\n• White — **белый** (*BYEH-ly*)\nRussian has two words for blue: **синий** (dark blue) and **голубой** (*gah-loo-BOY*, light blue)."],
  ["how do you say good morning in ukrainian | good morning in ukrainian | ukrainian for good morning", "In Ukrainian, good morning is **Доброго ранку** (*DOH-broh-hoh RAHN-koo*)."],
  ["how do you say good night in ukrainian | good night in ukrainian | goodnight in ukrainian", "In Ukrainian, good night is **На добраніч** (*nah doh-BRAH-neech*)."],
  ["how do you say how are you in ukrainian | how are you in ukrainian | ukrainian for how are you", "In Ukrainian, \"how are you?\" is **Як справи?** (*yahk SPRAH-vy*). Polite: **Як ся маєте?** (*yahk sya MAH-yeh-teh*). Reply: **Добре, дякую!** (*DOH-breh, DYAH-koo-yu*)"],
  ["how do you say my name is in ukrainian | my name is in ukrainian | what is your name in ukrainian", "In Ukrainian, \"my name is …\" is **Мене звати …** (*meh-NEH ZVAH-ty*) — just add your name. To ask: **Як тебе звати?** (*yahk teh-BEH ZVAH-ty*)"],
  ["how do you say i love you in ukrainian | i love you in ukrainian | ukrainian for i love you", "In Ukrainian, \"I love you\" is **Я тебе люблю** (*ya teh-BEH lyoo-BLYOO*). This is the everyday way to say it to family and friends. **Я тебе кохаю** (*ya teh-BEH koh-HAH-yu*) is romantic love."],
  ["how do you say happy birthday in ukrainian | happy birthday in ukrainian | ukrainian for happy birthday", "In Ukrainian, \"happy birthday\" is **З днем народження!** (*z dnem nah-ROH-dzheh-nya*)."],
  ["how do you say sorry in ukrainian | how do you say excuse me in ukrainian | sorry in ukrainian | excuse me in ukrainian", "In Ukrainian, \"excuse me\" is **Перепрошую** (*peh-reh-PROH-shoo-yu*) and \"sorry\" is **Вибачте** (*VY-bahch-teh*). With friends: **Вибач** (*VY-bahch*)."],
  ["how do you say where is the bathroom in ukrainian | where is the bathroom in ukrainian | where is the toilet in ukrainian", "In Ukrainian, \"where is the bathroom?\" is **Де туалет?** (*deh too-ah-LET*)."],
  ["how do you say i don't understand in ukrainian | i don't understand in ukrainian | i dont understand in ukrainian", "In Ukrainian, \"I don't understand\" is **Я не розумію** (*ya neh roh-zoo-MEE-yu*)."],
  ["how do you say do you speak english in ukrainian | do you speak english in ukrainian | how to ask if someone speaks english in ukrainian", "In Ukrainian, \"do you speak English?\" is **Ви говорите англійською?** (*vy hoh-VOH-ry-teh ahn-HLEEY-skoh-yu*)."],
  ["how do you say how much is this in ukrainian | how much is this in ukrainian | how much does it cost in ukrainian", "In Ukrainian, \"how much is this?\" is **Скільки це коштує?** (*SKEEL-ky tseh KOSH-too-yeh*)."],
  ["how do you say nice to meet you in ukrainian | nice to meet you in ukrainian | ukrainian for nice to meet you", "In Ukrainian, \"nice to meet you\" is **Приємно познайомитися** (*pry-YEM-noh poz-nah-YOH-my-ty-sya*). Short: **Дуже приємно** (*DOO-zheh pry-YEM-noh*, very nice)."],
  ["how do you say see you later in ukrainian | see you later in ukrainian | ukrainian for see you later", "In Ukrainian, \"see you later\" is **Побачимося пізніше** (*poh-BAH-chy-moh-sya peez-NEE-sheh*). Also **До зустрічі!** (*doh ZOOS-tree-chee*, see you!)."],
  ["count to ten in ukrainian | how do you count to 10 in ukrainian | numbers 1 to 10 in ukrainian", "Counting to ten in Ukrainian:\n1 — **один** (*oh-DYN*)\n2 — **два** (*dvah*)\n3 — **три** (*try*)\n4 — **чотири** (*choh-TY-ry*)\n5 — **п'ять** (*pyat*)\n6 — **шість** (*sheest*)\n7 — **сім** (*seem*)\n8 — **вісім** (*VEE-seem*)\n9 — **дев'ять** (*DEH-vyat*)\n10 — **десять** (*DEH-syat*)"],
  ["days of the week in ukrainian | how do you say monday in ukrainian | ukrainian days of the week", "The days of the week in Ukrainian:\n• Monday — **понеділок** (*poh-neh-DEE-lok*)\n• Tuesday — **вівторок** (*veev-TOH-rok*)\n• Wednesday — **середа** (*seh-reh-DAH*)\n• Thursday — **четвер** (*chet-VER*)\n• Friday — **п'ятниця** (*PYAT-ny-tsya*)\n• Saturday — **субота** (*soo-BOH-tah*)\n• Sunday — **неділя** (*neh-DEE-lya*)"],
  ["colors in ukrainian | colours in ukrainian | how do you say red in ukrainian", "Colors in Ukrainian:\n• Red — **червоний** (*cher-VOH-ny*)\n• Orange — **помаранчевий** (*poh-mah-RAHN-cheh-vy*)\n• Yellow — **жовтий** (*ZHOV-ty*)\n• Green — **зелений** (*zeh-LEH-ny*)\n• Blue — **синій** (*SY-neey*)\n• Purple — **фіолетовий** (*fee-oh-LEH-toh-vy*)\n• Black — **чорний** (*CHOR-ny*)\n• White — **білий** (*BEE-ly*)\nBlue and yellow (*синій і жовтий*) are the colors of Ukraine's flag — the sky above a wheat field."],
  ["how do you say good morning in arabic | good morning in arabic | arabic for good morning", "In Arabic, good morning is **صباح الخير** (*sa-BAAH al-KHAYR*). The classic reply is **صباح النور** (*sa-BAAH an-NOOR*, \"morning of light\")."],
  ["how do you say good night in arabic | good night in arabic | goodnight in arabic", "In Arabic, good night is **تصبح على خير** (*TUS-bih AA-la khayr*). Literally \"may you wake up well\". To a girl or woman: **تصبحين على خير** (*tus-bi-HEE-na AA-la khayr*)."],
  ["how do you say how are you in arabic | how are you in arabic | arabic for how are you", "In Arabic, \"how are you?\" is **كيف حالك؟** (*kayf HAA-lak*). To a girl or woman: *kayf HAA-lik*. A common reply is **الحمد لله، بخير** (*al-HAM-du lil-LAAH, bi-KHAYR*, \"thank God, fine\")."],
  ["how do you say my name is in arabic | my name is in arabic | what is your name in arabic", "In Arabic, \"my name is …\" is **اسمي …** (*IS-mee*) — just add your name. To ask: **ما اسمك؟** (*maa IS-muk*)"],
  ["how do you say i love you in arabic | i love you in arabic | arabic for i love you", "In Arabic, \"I love you\" is **أحبك** (*oo-HIB-buk*). To a girl or woman it's *oo-HIB-bu-ki*. It's said to family members too."],
  ["how do you say happy birthday in arabic | happy birthday in arabic | arabic for happy birthday", "In Arabic, \"happy birthday\" is **عيد ميلاد سعيد!** (*eed mee-LAAD sa-EED*)."],
  ["how do you say sorry in arabic | how do you say excuse me in arabic | sorry in arabic | excuse me in arabic", "In Arabic, \"excuse me\" is **لو سمحت** (*law sa-MAHT*) and \"sorry\" is **آسف** (*AA-sif*). A girl or woman says **آسفة** (*AA-si-fa*). **عفواً** (*AF-wan*) can also mean \"excuse me\"."],
  ["how do you say where is the bathroom in arabic | where is the bathroom in arabic | where is the toilet in arabic", "In Arabic, \"where is the bathroom?\" is **أين الحمام؟** (*AY-na al-ham-MAAM*)."],
  ["how do you say i don't understand in arabic | i don't understand in arabic | i dont understand in arabic", "In Arabic, \"I don't understand\" is **لا أفهم** (*laa AF-ham*)."],
  ["how do you say do you speak english in arabic | do you speak english in arabic | how to ask if someone speaks english in arabic", "In Arabic, \"do you speak English?\" is **هل تتكلم الإنجليزية؟** (*hal ta-ta-KAL-lam al-in-glee-ZEE-ya*)."],
  ["how do you say how much is this in arabic | how much is this in arabic | how much does it cost in arabic", "In Arabic, \"how much is this?\" is **بكم هذا؟** (*BI-kam HAA-thaa*)."],
  ["how do you say nice to meet you in arabic | nice to meet you in arabic | arabic for nice to meet you", "In Arabic, \"nice to meet you\" is **تشرفنا** (*ta-shar-RAF-naa*). Also **فرصة سعيدة** (*FUR-sa sa-EE-da*, \"a happy chance\")."],
  ["how do you say see you later in arabic | see you later in arabic | arabic for see you later", "In Arabic, \"see you later\" is **أراك لاحقاً** (*a-RAA-ka LAA-hi-qan*). Also **إلى اللقاء** (*i-la l-li-QAA*, until we meet again)."],
  ["count to ten in arabic | how do you count to 10 in arabic | numbers 1 to 10 in arabic", "Counting to ten in Arabic:\n1 — **واحد** (*WAA-hid*)\n2 — **اثنان** (*ith-NAAN*)\n3 — **ثلاثة** (*tha-LAA-tha*)\n4 — **أربعة** (*AR-ba-a*)\n5 — **خمسة** (*KHAM-sa*)\n6 — **ستة** (*SIT-ta*)\n7 — **سبعة** (*SAB-a*)\n8 — **ثمانية** (*tha-MAA-ni-ya*)\n9 — **تسعة** (*TIS-a*)\n10 — **عشرة** (*ASH-ra*)\nArabic is written right to left, and many countries use the digits ١ ٢ ٣ ٤ ٥ ٦ ٧ ٨ ٩ ١٠."],
  ["days of the week in arabic | how do you say monday in arabic | arabic days of the week", "The days of the week in Arabic:\n• Monday — **الاثنين** (*al-ith-NAYN*)\n• Tuesday — **الثلاثاء** (*ath-tha-laa-THAA*)\n• Wednesday — **الأربعاء** (*al-ar-bi-AA*)\n• Thursday — **الخميس** (*al-kha-MEES*)\n• Friday — **الجمعة** (*al-JUM-a*)\n• Saturday — **السبت** (*as-SABT*)\n• Sunday — **الأحد** (*al-A-had*)\nMany Arabic-speaking countries start the week on Sunday (*al-ahad*, \"day one\"), and Friday is the main day off."],
  ["colors in arabic | colours in arabic | how do you say red in arabic", "Colors in Arabic:\n• Red — **أحمر** (*AH-mar*)\n• Orange — **برتقالي** (*bur-tu-QAA-lee*)\n• Yellow — **أصفر** (*AS-far*)\n• Green — **أخضر** (*AKH-dar*)\n• Blue — **أزرق** (*AZ-raq*)\n• Purple — **بنفسجي** (*ba-naf-SA-jee*)\n• Black — **أسود** (*AS-wad*)\n• White — **أبيض** (*AB-yad*)\n*Burtuqali* (orange) comes from *burtuqal*, the fruit."],
  ["how do you say good morning in hebrew | good morning in hebrew | hebrew for good morning", "In Hebrew, good morning is **בוקר טוב** (*BOH-ker tov*). A friendly reply is **בוקר אור** (*BOH-ker or*, \"morning of light\")."],
  ["how do you say good night in hebrew | good night in hebrew | goodnight in hebrew", "In Hebrew, good night is **לילה טוב** (*LAI-lah tov*)."],
  ["how do you say how are you in hebrew | how are you in hebrew | hebrew for how are you", "In Hebrew, \"how are you?\" is **מה שלומך?** (*mah shlom-KHA*). That's to a boy or man; to a girl or woman say *mah shlo-MEKH*. Casual: **מה נשמע?** (*mah nish-MA*, \"what's up?\")."],
  ["how do you say my name is in hebrew | my name is in hebrew | what is your name in hebrew", "In Hebrew, \"my name is …\" is **קוראים לי …** (*kor-EEM lee*) — just add your name. Also **השם שלי …** (*ha-SHEM sheh-LEE*). To ask: **איך קוראים לך?** (*eykh kor-EEM le-KHA*)"],
  ["how do you say i love you in hebrew | i love you in hebrew | hebrew for i love you", "In Hebrew, \"I love you\" is **אני אוהב אותך** (*a-NEE oh-HEV ot-KHA*). Hebrew changes with gender: a girl or woman says *oh-HE-vet* instead of *oh-HEV*, and to a girl or woman you say *o-TAKH* instead of *ot-KHA*."],
  ["how do you say happy birthday in hebrew | happy birthday in hebrew | hebrew for happy birthday", "In Hebrew, \"happy birthday\" is **יום הולדת שמח!** (*yom hu-LE-det sa-MEI-akh*). Also **מזל טוב!** (*ma-ZAL tov*, congratulations!)."],
  ["how do you say sorry in hebrew | how do you say excuse me in hebrew | sorry in hebrew | excuse me in hebrew", "In Hebrew, **סליחה** (*slee-KHA*) means both \"excuse me\" and \"sorry\". For a bigger apology: **אני מצטער** (*a-NEE mits-ta-ER*); a girl or woman says **מצטערת** (*mits-ta-E-ret*)."],
  ["how do you say where is the bathroom in hebrew | where is the bathroom in hebrew | where is the toilet in hebrew", "In Hebrew, \"where is the bathroom?\" is **איפה השירותים?** (*EI-fo ha-shey-ru-TEEM*)."],
  ["how do you say i don't understand in hebrew | i don't understand in hebrew | i dont understand in hebrew", "In Hebrew, \"I don't understand\" is **אני לא מבין** (*a-NEE lo me-VEEN*). A girl or woman says **מבינה** (*me-vee-NA*)."],
  ["how do you say do you speak english in hebrew | do you speak english in hebrew | how to ask if someone speaks english in hebrew", "In Hebrew, \"do you speak English?\" is **אתה מדבר אנגלית?** (*a-TA me-da-BER ANG-leet*). To a girl or woman: **את מדברת אנגלית?** (*at me-da-BE-ret ANG-leet*)"],
  ["how do you say how much is this in hebrew | how much is this in hebrew | how much does it cost in hebrew", "In Hebrew, \"how much is this?\" is **כמה זה עולה?** (*KAH-ma ze o-LE*)."],
  ["how do you say nice to meet you in hebrew | nice to meet you in hebrew | hebrew for nice to meet you", "In Hebrew, \"nice to meet you\" is **נעים מאוד** (*na-EEM me-OD*)."],
  ["how do you say see you later in hebrew | see you later in hebrew | hebrew for see you later", "In Hebrew, \"see you later\" is **נתראה אחר כך** (*nit-ra-E a-KHAR kakh*). Also **להתראות** (*le-hit-ra-OT*, see you / goodbye)."],
  ["count to ten in hebrew | how do you count to 10 in hebrew | numbers 1 to 10 in hebrew", "Counting to ten in Hebrew:\n1 — **אחת** (*a-KHAT*)\n2 — **שתיים** (*SHTA-yim*)\n3 — **שלוש** (*sha-LOSH*)\n4 — **ארבע** (*AR-ba*)\n5 — **חמש** (*kha-MESH*)\n6 — **שש** (*shesh*)\n7 — **שבע** (*SHE-va*)\n8 — **שמונה** (*shmo-NE*)\n9 — **תשע** (*TE-sha*)\n10 — **עשר** (*E-ser*)\nHebrew is written right to left, and these are the forms people use for counting."],
  ["days of the week in hebrew | how do you say monday in hebrew | hebrew days of the week", "The days of the week in Hebrew:\n• Monday — **יום שני** (*yom shey-NEE*)\n• Tuesday — **יום שלישי** (*yom shlee-SHEE*)\n• Wednesday — **יום רביעי** (*yom re-vee-EE*)\n• Thursday — **יום חמישי** (*yom kha-mee-SHEE*)\n• Friday — **יום שישי** (*yom shee-SHEE*)\n• Saturday — **שבת** (*sha-BAT*)\n• Sunday — **יום ראשון** (*yom ree-SHON*)\nThe days are numbered: Sunday is \"day one\", Monday \"day two\", and so on. Saturday is *Shabbat*, the day of rest."],
  ["colors in hebrew | colours in hebrew | how do you say red in hebrew", "Colors in Hebrew:\n• Red — **אדום** (*a-DOM*)\n• Orange — **כתום** (*ka-TOM*)\n• Yellow — **צהוב** (*tsa-HOV*)\n• Green — **ירוק** (*ya-ROK*)\n• Blue — **כחול** (*ka-KHOL*)\n• Purple — **סגול** (*sa-GOL*)\n• Black — **שחור** (*sha-KHOR*)\n• White — **לבן** (*la-VAN*)"],
  ["how do you say good morning in hindi | good morning in hindi | hindi for good morning", "In Hindi, good morning is **सुप्रभात** (*su-pra-BHAAT*). Day to day, most people just say **नमस्ते** (*na-mas-TAY*) at any time."],
  ["how do you say good night in hindi | good night in hindi | goodnight in hindi", "In Hindi, good night is **शुभ रात्रि** (*shubh RAA-tri*)."],
  ["how do you say how are you in hindi | how are you in hindi | hindi for how are you", "In Hindi, \"how are you?\" is **आप कैसे हैं?** (*aap KAI-se hain*). To a woman: **आप कैसी हैं?** (*aap KAI-see hain*). Casual: **क्या हाल है?** (*kyaa haal hai*). Reply: **मैं ठीक हूँ** (*main theek hoon*, I'm fine)."],
  ["how do you say my name is in hindi | my name is in hindi | what is your name in hindi", "In Hindi, \"my name is …\" is **मेरा नाम … है** (*MAY-raa naam … hai*) — just add your name. To ask: **आपका नाम क्या है?** (*AAP-kaa naam kyaa hai*)"],
  ["how do you say i love you in hindi | i love you in hindi | hindi for i love you", "In Hindi, \"I love you\" is **मैं तुमसे प्यार करता हूँ** (*main TUM-se pyaar KAR-taa hoon*). A girl or woman says **करती** (*KAR-tee*) instead of करता. Kids often just say **I love you, Mummy!** in English, too."],
  ["how do you say happy birthday in hindi | happy birthday in hindi | hindi for happy birthday", "In Hindi, \"happy birthday\" is **जन्मदिन मुबारक हो!** (*JANM-din mu-BAA-rak ho*). Also **जन्मदिन की शुभकामनाएँ** (*JANM-din kee shubh-kaam-NAA-en*, birthday wishes)."],
  ["how do you say sorry in hindi | how do you say excuse me in hindi | sorry in hindi | excuse me in hindi", "In Hindi, \"excuse me\" is **सुनिए** (*SU-ni-ye*) and \"sorry\" is **माफ़ कीजिए** (*maaf KEE-ji-ye*). *Suniye* literally means \"please listen\" and is used to get someone's attention. Many people also say the English word **sorry**."],
  ["how do you say where is the bathroom in hindi | where is the bathroom in hindi | where is the toilet in hindi", "In Hindi, \"where is the bathroom?\" is **बाथरूम कहाँ है?** (*BAATH-room ka-HAAN hai*). More formal: **शौचालय कहाँ है?** (*shau-CHAA-lay ka-HAAN hai*)"],
  ["how do you say i don't understand in hindi | i don't understand in hindi | i dont understand in hindi", "In Hindi, \"I don't understand\" is **मुझे समझ नहीं आया** (*mu-JHE sa-MAJH na-HEEN AA-yaa*)."],
  ["how do you say do you speak english in hindi | do you speak english in hindi | how to ask if someone speaks english in hindi", "In Hindi, \"do you speak English?\" is **क्या आप अंग्रेज़ी बोलते हैं?** (*kyaa aap an-GREZ-ee BOL-te hain*). To a woman: **बोलती** (*BOL-tee*) instead of बोलते."],
  ["how do you say how much is this in hindi | how much is this in hindi | how much does it cost in hindi", "In Hindi, \"how much is this?\" is **यह कितने का है?** (*yeh KIT-ne kaa hai*)."],
  ["how do you say nice to meet you in hindi | nice to meet you in hindi | hindi for nice to meet you", "In Hindi, \"nice to meet you\" is **आपसे मिलकर ख़ुशी हुई** (*AAP-se MIL-kar khu-SHEE hu-EE*)."],
  ["how do you say see you later in hindi | see you later in hindi | hindi for see you later", "In Hindi, \"see you later\" is **फिर मिलेंगे** (*phir mi-LEN-ge*). Literally \"we'll meet again\"."],
  ["count to ten in hindi | how do you count to 10 in hindi | numbers 1 to 10 in hindi", "Counting to ten in Hindi:\n1 — **एक** (*ek*)\n2 — **दो** (*do*)\n3 — **तीन** (*teen*)\n4 — **चार** (*chaar*)\n5 — **पाँच** (*paanch*)\n6 — **छह** (*chhe*)\n7 — **सात** (*saat*)\n8 — **आठ** (*aath*)\n9 — **नौ** (*nau*)\n10 — **दस** (*das*)\nHindi is written in the Devanagari script."],
  ["days of the week in hindi | how do you say monday in hindi | hindi days of the week", "The days of the week in Hindi:\n• Monday — **सोमवार** (*SOM-vaar*)\n• Tuesday — **मंगलवार** (*MAN-gal-vaar*)\n• Wednesday — **बुधवार** (*BUDH-vaar*)\n• Thursday — **गुरुवार** (*GU-ru-vaar*)\n• Friday — **शुक्रवार** (*SHUK-ra-vaar*)\n• Saturday — **शनिवार** (*SHA-ni-vaar*)\n• Sunday — **रविवार** (*RA-vi-vaar*)\n*Vaar* means \"day\". *Som* is the Moon and *Ravi* is the Sun — just like Monday and Sunday in English!"],
  ["colors in hindi | colours in hindi | how do you say red in hindi", "Colors in Hindi:\n• Red — **लाल** (*laal*)\n• Orange — **नारंगी** (*naa-RAN-gee*)\n• Yellow — **पीला** (*PEE-laa*)\n• Green — **हरा** (*HA-raa*)\n• Blue — **नीला** (*NEE-laa*)\n• Purple — **बैंगनी** (*BAING-nee*)\n• Black — **काला** (*KAA-laa*)\n• White — **सफ़ेद** (*sa-FED*)\n*Baingani* (purple) comes from *baingan*, the eggplant!"],
  ["how do you say good morning in bengali | good morning in bengali | bengali for good morning | good morning in bangla", "In Bengali, good morning is **সুপ্রভাত** (*shu-pro-BHAT*). Day to day, people often just say **নমস্কার** (*no-mosh-KAR*) or **আসসালামু আলাইকুম** (*as-sa-LA-mu a-LAI-kum*)."],
  ["how do you say good night in bengali | good night in bengali | goodnight in bengali | good night in bangla", "In Bengali, good night is **শুভ রাত্রি** (*shu-bho RA-tri*)."],
  ["how do you say how are you in bengali | how are you in bengali | bengali for how are you | how are you in bangla", "In Bengali, \"how are you?\" is **আপনি কেমন আছেন?** (*AP-ni KE-mon A-chhen*). Casual: **কেমন আছো?** (*KE-mon A-chho*). Reply: **ভালো আছি** (*BHA-lo A-chhi*, I'm fine)."],
  ["how do you say my name is in bengali | my name is in bengali | what is your name in bengali | how do you say my name is in bangla", "In Bengali, \"my name is …\" is **আমার নাম …** (*A-mar nam*) — just add your name. To ask: **আপনার নাম কী?** (*AP-nar nam KI*)"],
  ["how do you say i love you in bengali | i love you in bengali | bengali for i love you | i love you in bangla", "In Bengali, \"I love you\" is **আমি তোমাকে ভালোবাসি** (*A-mi TO-ma-ke BHA-lo-ba-shi*). Said to family as well as sweethearts."],
  ["how do you say happy birthday in bengali | happy birthday in bengali | bengali for happy birthday | happy birthday in bangla", "In Bengali, \"happy birthday\" is **শুভ জন্মদিন!** (*shu-bho JON-mo-din*)."],
  ["how do you say sorry in bengali | how do you say excuse me in bengali | sorry in bengali | excuse me in bengali", "In Bengali, \"excuse me\" is **শুনুন** (*SHU-nun*) and \"sorry\" is **দুঃখিত** (*DUKH-khi-to*). *Shunun* literally means \"please listen\" and is used to get someone's attention. Many people also say the English word **sorry**."],
  ["how do you say where is the bathroom in bengali | where is the bathroom in bengali | where is the toilet in bengali | where is the bathroom in bangla", "In Bengali, \"where is the bathroom?\" is **বাথরুম কোথায়?** (*BATH-room KO-thay*)."],
  ["how do you say i don't understand in bengali | i don't understand in bengali | i dont understand in bengali | i don't understand in bangla", "In Bengali, \"I don't understand\" is **আমি বুঝতে পারছি না** (*A-mi BUJH-te PAR-chhi na*)."],
  ["how do you say do you speak english in bengali | do you speak english in bengali | how to ask if someone speaks english in bengali | do you speak english in bangla", "In Bengali, \"do you speak English?\" is **আপনি কি ইংরেজি বলতে পারেন?** (*AP-ni ki ING-re-ji BOL-te PA-ren*)."],
  ["how do you say how much is this in bengali | how much is this in bengali | how much does it cost in bengali | how much is this in bangla", "In Bengali, \"how much is this?\" is **এটার দাম কত?** (*E-tar dam KO-to*)."],
  ["how do you say nice to meet you in bengali | nice to meet you in bengali | bengali for nice to meet you | nice to meet you in bangla", "In Bengali, \"nice to meet you\" is **আপনার সাথে দেখা হয়ে ভালো লাগলো** (*AP-nar SHA-the DE-kha HO-ye BHA-lo LAG-lo*)."],
  ["how do you say see you later in bengali | see you later in bengali | bengali for see you later | see you later in bangla", "In Bengali, \"see you later\" is **পরে দেখা হবে** (*PO-re DE-kha HO-be*)."],
  ["count to ten in bengali | how do you count to 10 in bengali | numbers 1 to 10 in bengali | count to ten in bangla", "Counting to ten in Bengali:\n1 — **এক** (*ek*)\n2 — **দুই** (*dui*)\n3 — **তিন** (*tin*)\n4 — **চার** (*char*)\n5 — **পাঁচ** (*panch*)\n6 — **ছয়** (*chhoy*)\n7 — **সাত** (*shat*)\n8 — **আট** (*at*)\n9 — **নয়** (*noy*)\n10 — **দশ** (*dosh*)\nBengali has its own digits too: ১ ২ ৩ ৪ ৫ ৬ ৭ ৮ ৯ ১০."],
  ["days of the week in bengali | how do you say monday in bengali | bengali days of the week | days of the week in bangla", "The days of the week in Bengali:\n• Monday — **সোমবার** (*SHOM-bar*)\n• Tuesday — **মঙ্গলবার** (*MON-gol-bar*)\n• Wednesday — **বুধবার** (*BUDH-bar*)\n• Thursday — **বৃহস্পতিবার** (*bri-HOSH-po-ti-bar*)\n• Friday — **শুক্রবার** (*SHUK-ro-bar*)\n• Saturday — **শনিবার** (*SHO-ni-bar*)\n• Sunday — **রবিবার** (*RO-bi-bar*)"],
  ["colors in bengali | colours in bengali | how do you say red in bengali | colors in bangla", "Colors in Bengali:\n• Red — **লাল** (*lal*)\n• Orange — **কমলা** (*KOM-la*)\n• Yellow — **হলুদ** (*HO-lud*)\n• Green — **সবুজ** (*SHO-buj*)\n• Blue — **নীল** (*nil*)\n• Purple — **বেগুনি** (*BE-gu-ni*)\n• Black — **কালো** (*KA-lo*)\n• White — **সাদা** (*SHA-da*)\n*Komla* (orange) is also the word for the fruit, and *holud* (yellow) is also turmeric."],
  ["how do you say good morning in urdu | good morning in urdu | urdu for good morning", "In Urdu, good morning is **صبح بخیر** (*su-bah ba-KHAIR*). Day to day, most people greet with **السلام علیکم** (*as-sa-LAA-mu a-LAI-kum*) at any time."],
  ["how do you say good night in urdu | good night in urdu | goodnight in urdu", "In Urdu, good night is **شب بخیر** (*shab ba-KHAIR*)."],
  ["how do you say how are you in urdu | how are you in urdu | urdu for how are you", "In Urdu, \"how are you?\" is **آپ کیسے ہیں؟** (*aap KAI-se hain*). To a woman: **آپ کیسی ہیں؟** (*aap KAI-see hain*). Casual: **کیا حال ہے؟** (*kyaa haal hai*)"],
  ["how do you say my name is in urdu | my name is in urdu | what is your name in urdu", "In Urdu, \"my name is …\" is **میرا نام … ہے** (*MAY-raa naam … hai*) — just add your name. To ask: **آپ کا نام کیا ہے؟** (*aap kaa naam kyaa hai*)"],
  ["how do you say i love you in urdu | i love you in urdu | urdu for i love you", "In Urdu, \"I love you\" is **میں تم سے پیار کرتا ہوں** (*main tum se pyaar KAR-taa hoon*). A girl or woman says **کرتی ہوں** (*KAR-tee hoon*)."],
  ["how do you say happy birthday in urdu | happy birthday in urdu | urdu for happy birthday", "In Urdu, \"happy birthday\" is **سالگرہ مبارک!** (*saal-gi-RAH mu-BAA-rak*)."],
  ["how do you say sorry in urdu | how do you say excuse me in urdu | sorry in urdu | excuse me in urdu", "In Urdu, \"excuse me\" is **سنیے** (*SU-ni-ye*) and \"sorry\" is **معاف کیجیے** (*maaf KEE-ji-ye*). *Suniye* literally means \"please listen\" and is used to get someone's attention."],
  ["how do you say where is the bathroom in urdu | where is the bathroom in urdu | where is the toilet in urdu", "In Urdu, \"where is the bathroom?\" is **واش روم کہاں ہے؟** (*WAASH-room ka-HAAN hai*). In Pakistan the bathroom is usually called the \"washroom\"."],
  ["how do you say i don't understand in urdu | i don't understand in urdu | i dont understand in urdu", "In Urdu, \"I don't understand\" is **مجھے سمجھ نہیں آیا** (*mu-JHE sa-MAJH na-HEEN AA-yaa*)."],
  ["how do you say do you speak english in urdu | do you speak english in urdu | how to ask if someone speaks english in urdu", "In Urdu, \"do you speak English?\" is **کیا آپ انگریزی بولتے ہیں؟** (*kyaa aap an-GREZ-ee BOL-te hain*)."],
  ["how do you say how much is this in urdu | how much is this in urdu | how much does it cost in urdu", "In Urdu, \"how much is this?\" is **یہ کتنے کا ہے؟** (*yeh KIT-ne kaa hai*)."],
  ["how do you say nice to meet you in urdu | nice to meet you in urdu | urdu for nice to meet you", "In Urdu, \"nice to meet you\" is **آپ سے مل کر خوشی ہوئی** (*aap se mil kar khu-SHEE hu-EE*)."],
  ["how do you say see you later in urdu | see you later in urdu | urdu for see you later", "In Urdu, \"see you later\" is **پھر ملیں گے** (*phir mi-LEN-ge*). Literally \"we'll meet again\"."],
  ["count to ten in urdu | how do you count to 10 in urdu | numbers 1 to 10 in urdu", "Counting to ten in Urdu:\n1 — **ایک** (*ek*)\n2 — **دو** (*do*)\n3 — **تین** (*teen*)\n4 — **چار** (*chaar*)\n5 — **پانچ** (*paanch*)\n6 — **چھ** (*chhe*)\n7 — **سات** (*saat*)\n8 — **آٹھ** (*aath*)\n9 — **نو** (*nau*)\n10 — **دس** (*das*)\nUrdu is written right to left in the Nastaliq style of the Perso-Arabic script. Spoken Urdu sounds a lot like Hindi!"],
  ["days of the week in urdu | how do you say monday in urdu | urdu days of the week", "The days of the week in Urdu:\n• Monday — **پیر** (*peer*)\n• Tuesday — **منگل** (*MAN-gal*)\n• Wednesday — **بدھ** (*budh*)\n• Thursday — **جمعرات** (*ju-me-RAAT*)\n• Friday — **جمعہ** (*JU-maa*)\n• Saturday — **ہفتہ** (*HAF-taa*)\n• Sunday — **اتوار** (*it-VAAR*)"],
  ["colors in urdu | colours in urdu | how do you say red in urdu", "Colors in Urdu:\n• Red — **لال** (*laal*)\n• Orange — **نارنجی** (*naa-RAN-jee*)\n• Yellow — **پیلا** (*PEE-laa*)\n• Green — **ہرا** (*HA-raa*)\n• Blue — **نیلا** (*NEE-laa*)\n• Purple — **جامنی** (*JAA-mu-nee*)\n• Black — **کالا** (*KAA-laa*)\n• White — **سفید** (*sa-FED*)"],
  ["how do you say good morning in chinese | good morning in chinese | chinese for good morning | good morning in mandarin", "In Mandarin Chinese, good morning is **早上好** (*zǎoshang hǎo*). Short and casual: **早！** (*zǎo*)"],
  ["how do you say good night in chinese | good night in chinese | goodnight in chinese | good night in mandarin", "In Mandarin Chinese, good night is **晚安** (*wǎn'ān*)."],
  ["how do you say how are you in chinese | how are you in chinese | chinese for how are you | how are you in mandarin", "In Mandarin Chinese, \"how are you?\" is **你好吗？** (*nǐ hǎo ma*). People also ask **最近怎么样？** (*zuìjìn zěnmeyàng*, \"how have you been lately?\"). Reply: **我很好** (*wǒ hěn hǎo*, I'm fine)."],
  ["how do you say my name is in chinese | my name is in chinese | what is your name in chinese | how do you say my name is in mandarin", "In Mandarin Chinese, \"my name is …\" is **我叫…** (*wǒ jiào*) — just add your name. To ask: **你叫什么名字？** (*nǐ jiào shénme míngzi*)"],
  ["how do you say i love you in chinese | i love you in chinese | chinese for i love you | i love you in mandarin", "In Mandarin Chinese, \"I love you\" is **我爱你** (*wǒ ài nǐ*). Chinese families often show love more through actions than words, but **我爱你** is understood everywhere."],
  ["how do you say happy birthday in chinese | happy birthday in chinese | chinese for happy birthday | happy birthday in mandarin", "In Mandarin Chinese, \"happy birthday\" is **生日快乐！** (*shēngrì kuàilè*)."],
  ["how do you say sorry in chinese | how do you say excuse me in chinese | sorry in chinese | excuse me in chinese", "In Mandarin Chinese, \"excuse me\" is **打扰一下** (*dǎrǎo yíxià*) and \"sorry\" is **对不起** (*duìbuqǐ*). For small things, **不好意思** (*bù hǎoyìsi*) works as both \"excuse me\" and \"sorry\"."],
  ["how do you say where is the bathroom in chinese | where is the bathroom in chinese | where is the toilet in chinese | where is the bathroom in mandarin", "In Mandarin Chinese, \"where is the bathroom?\" is **洗手间在哪里？** (*xǐshǒujiān zài nǎlǐ*)."],
  ["how do you say i don't understand in chinese | i don't understand in chinese | i dont understand in chinese | i don't understand in mandarin", "In Mandarin Chinese, \"I don't understand\" is **我听不懂** (*wǒ tīng bu dǒng*). That means \"I can't understand what I'm hearing\". Also **我不明白** (*wǒ bù míngbai*)."],
  ["how do you say do you speak english in chinese | do you speak english in chinese | how to ask if someone speaks english in chinese | do you speak english in mandarin", "In Mandarin Chinese, \"do you speak English?\" is **你会说英语吗？** (*nǐ huì shuō Yīngyǔ ma*)."],
  ["how do you say how much is this in chinese | how much is this in chinese | how much does it cost in chinese | how much is this in mandarin", "In Mandarin Chinese, \"how much is this?\" is **这个多少钱？** (*zhège duōshao qián*)."],
  ["how do you say nice to meet you in chinese | nice to meet you in chinese | chinese for nice to meet you | nice to meet you in mandarin", "In Mandarin Chinese, \"nice to meet you\" is **很高兴认识你** (*hěn gāoxìng rènshi nǐ*)."],
  ["how do you say see you later in chinese | see you later in chinese | chinese for see you later | see you later in mandarin", "In Mandarin Chinese, \"see you later\" is **回头见** (*huítóu jiàn*). Also **待会儿见** (*dāihuìr jiàn*, see you in a bit) and **明天见** (*míngtiān jiàn*, see you tomorrow)."],
  ["count to ten in chinese | how do you count to 10 in chinese | numbers 1 to 10 in chinese | count to ten in mandarin", "Counting to ten in Mandarin Chinese:\n1 — **一** (*yī*)\n2 — **二** (*èr*)\n3 — **三** (*sān*)\n4 — **四** (*sì*)\n5 — **五** (*wǔ*)\n6 — **六** (*liù*)\n7 — **七** (*qī*)\n8 — **八** (*bā*)\n9 — **九** (*jiǔ*)\n10 — **十** (*shí*)\nThe marks on the pinyin show the four tones — they change the meaning!"],
  ["days of the week in chinese | how do you say monday in chinese | chinese days of the week | days of the week in mandarin", "The days of the week in Mandarin Chinese:\n• Monday — **星期一** (*xīngqī yī*)\n• Tuesday — **星期二** (*xīngqī èr*)\n• Wednesday — **星期三** (*xīngqī sān*)\n• Thursday — **星期四** (*xīngqī sì*)\n• Friday — **星期五** (*xīngqī wǔ*)\n• Saturday — **星期六** (*xīngqī liù*)\n• Sunday — **星期天** (*xīngqī tiān*)\nEasy pattern: Monday is \"week one\", Tuesday \"week two\" and so on. Sunday is also written **星期日** (*xīngqī rì*)."],
  ["colors in chinese | colours in chinese | how do you say red in chinese | colors in mandarin", "Colors in Mandarin Chinese:\n• Red — **红色** (*hóngsè*)\n• Orange — **橙色** (*chéngsè*)\n• Yellow — **黄色** (*huángsè*)\n• Green — **绿色** (*lǜsè*)\n• Blue — **蓝色** (*lánsè*)\n• Purple — **紫色** (*zǐsè*)\n• Black — **黑色** (*hēisè*)\n• White — **白色** (*báisè*)\n**色** (*sè*) means \"color\". Red is a lucky color in China."],
  ["how do you say good morning in japanese | good morning in japanese | japanese for good morning", "In Japanese, good morning is **おはようございます** (*ohayō gozaimasu*). With friends you can just say **おはよう** (*ohayō*)."],
  ["how do you say good night in japanese | good night in japanese | goodnight in japanese", "In Japanese, good night is **おやすみなさい** (*oyasuminasai*). Casually: **おやすみ** (*oyasumi*). Good evening is **こんばんは** (*konbanwa*)."],
  ["how do you say how are you in japanese | how are you in japanese | japanese for how are you", "In Japanese, \"how are you?\" is **お元気ですか？** (*o-genki desu ka*). Reply: **元気です** (*genki desu*, I'm fine). It's mostly asked when you haven't seen someone for a while."],
  ["how do you say my name is in japanese | my name is in japanese | what is your name in japanese", "In Japanese, \"my name is …\" is **私の名前は…です** (*watashi no namae wa … desu*) — just add your name. Shorter and very common: **…です** (*… desu*). To ask: **お名前は？** (*o-namae wa?*)"],
  ["how do you say i love you in japanese | i love you in japanese | japanese for i love you", "In Japanese, \"I love you\" is **大好き** (*daisuki*). Literally \"I like you so much\", it's the warm way people say it to family and friends. **愛してる** (*aishiteru*) is deep romantic love and is rarely said out loud."],
  ["how do you say happy birthday in japanese | happy birthday in japanese | japanese for happy birthday", "In Japanese, \"happy birthday\" is **お誕生日おめでとうございます！** (*o-tanjōbi omedetō gozaimasu*). With friends: **お誕生日おめでとう！** (*o-tanjōbi omedetō*)"],
  ["how do you say sorry in japanese | how do you say excuse me in japanese | sorry in japanese | excuse me in japanese", "In Japanese, \"excuse me\" is **すみません** (*sumimasen*) and \"sorry\" is **ごめんなさい** (*gomen nasai*). **すみません** also works as a polite \"sorry\" — and even as \"thanks for your trouble\"."],
  ["how do you say where is the bathroom in japanese | where is the bathroom in japanese | where is the toilet in japanese", "In Japanese, \"where is the bathroom?\" is **トイレはどこですか？** (*toire wa doko desu ka*)."],
  ["how do you say i don't understand in japanese | i don't understand in japanese | i dont understand in japanese", "In Japanese, \"I don't understand\" is **わかりません** (*wakarimasen*)."],
  ["how do you say do you speak english in japanese | do you speak english in japanese | how to ask if someone speaks english in japanese", "In Japanese, \"do you speak English?\" is **英語を話せますか？** (*eigo o hanasemasu ka*)."],
  ["how do you say how much is this in japanese | how much is this in japanese | how much does it cost in japanese", "In Japanese, \"how much is this?\" is **これはいくらですか？** (*kore wa ikura desu ka*)."],
  ["how do you say nice to meet you in japanese | nice to meet you in japanese | japanese for nice to meet you", "In Japanese, \"nice to meet you\" is **はじめまして** (*hajimemashite*). Usually followed by **よろしくお願いします** (*yoroshiku onegaishimasu*)."],
  ["how do you say see you later in japanese | see you later in japanese | japanese for see you later", "In Japanese, \"see you later\" is **またあとで** (*mata ato de*). Also **またね！** (*mata ne*, see you!)."],
  ["count to ten in japanese | how do you count to 10 in japanese | numbers 1 to 10 in japanese", "Counting to ten in Japanese:\n1 — **一 いち** (*ichi*)\n2 — **二 に** (*ni*)\n3 — **三 さん** (*san*)\n4 — **四 よん** (*yon*)\n5 — **五 ご** (*go*)\n6 — **六 ろく** (*roku*)\n7 — **七 なな** (*nana*)\n8 — **八 はち** (*hachi*)\n9 — **九 きゅう** (*kyū*)\n10 — **十 じゅう** (*jū*)\nFour and seven also have the readings *shi* and *shichi*."],
  ["days of the week in japanese | how do you say monday in japanese | japanese days of the week", "The days of the week in Japanese:\n• Monday — **月曜日** (*getsuyōbi*)\n• Tuesday — **火曜日** (*kayōbi*)\n• Wednesday — **水曜日** (*suiyōbi*)\n• Thursday — **木曜日** (*mokuyōbi*)\n• Friday — **金曜日** (*kin'yōbi*)\n• Saturday — **土曜日** (*doyōbi*)\n• Sunday — **日曜日** (*nichiyōbi*)\nThe days are named after the moon, fire, water, wood, gold, earth and sun."],
  ["colors in japanese | colours in japanese | how do you say red in japanese", "Colors in Japanese:\n• Red — **赤** (*aka*)\n• Orange — **オレンジ** (*orenji*)\n• Yellow — **黄色** (*kiiro*)\n• Green — **緑** (*midori*)\n• Blue — **青** (*ao*)\n• Purple — **紫** (*murasaki*)\n• Black — **黒** (*kuro*)\n• White — **白** (*shiro*)\nIn Japan a green traffic light is called **青** (*ao*, blue)!"],
  ["how do you say good morning in korean | good morning in korean | korean for good morning", "In Korean, good morning is **좋은 아침이에요** (*jo-eun achim-ieyo*). Day to day, Koreans usually just say **안녕하세요** (*annyeonghaseyo*) at any time."],
  ["how do you say good night in korean | good night in korean | goodnight in korean", "In Korean, good night is **안녕히 주무세요** (*annyeonghi jumuseyo*). That's polite, for grown-ups. With friends: **잘 자** (*jal ja*)."],
  ["how do you say how are you in korean | how are you in korean | korean for how are you", "In Korean, \"how are you?\" is **잘 지내요?** (*jal jinaeyo*). Also **잘 지내셨어요?** (*jal jinaesyeosseoyo*, how have you been?). Reply: **네, 잘 지내요** (*ne, jal jinaeyo*)."],
  ["how do you say my name is in korean | my name is in korean | what is your name in korean", "In Korean, \"my name is …\" is **제 이름은 …이에요** (*je ireumeun … ieyo*) — just add your name. After a name ending in a vowel, use **…예요** (*yeyo*). To ask: **이름이 뭐예요?** (*ireumi mwoyeyo*)"],
  ["how do you say i love you in korean | i love you in korean | korean for i love you", "In Korean, \"I love you\" is **사랑해요** (*saranghaeyo*). Casual: **사랑해** (*saranghae*). Koreans say it to family a lot, too!"],
  ["how do you say happy birthday in korean | happy birthday in korean | korean for happy birthday", "In Korean, \"happy birthday\" is **생일 축하해요!** (*saengil chukahaeyo*). Casual: **생일 축하해!** (*saengil chukahae*)"],
  ["how do you say sorry in korean | how do you say excuse me in korean | sorry in korean | excuse me in korean", "In Korean, \"excuse me\" is **실례합니다** (*sillyehamnida*) and \"sorry\" is **죄송합니다** (*joesonghamnida*). Less formal sorry: **미안해요** (*mianhaeyo*). To call a waiter, say **저기요** (*jeogiyo*)."],
  ["how do you say where is the bathroom in korean | where is the bathroom in korean | where is the toilet in korean", "In Korean, \"where is the bathroom?\" is **화장실이 어디예요?** (*hwajangsiri eodiyeyo*)."],
  ["how do you say i don't understand in korean | i don't understand in korean | i dont understand in korean", "In Korean, \"I don't understand\" is **이해가 안 돼요** (*ihaega an dwaeyo*). Also **잘 모르겠어요** (*jal moreugesseoyo*, I'm not sure)."],
  ["how do you say do you speak english in korean | do you speak english in korean | how to ask if someone speaks english in korean", "In Korean, \"do you speak English?\" is **영어 할 줄 아세요?** (*yeong-eo hal jul aseyo*)."],
  ["how do you say how much is this in korean | how much is this in korean | how much does it cost in korean", "In Korean, \"how much is this?\" is **이거 얼마예요?** (*igeo eolmayeyo*)."],
  ["how do you say nice to meet you in korean | nice to meet you in korean | korean for nice to meet you", "In Korean, \"nice to meet you\" is **만나서 반가워요** (*mannaseo bangawoyo*). More formal: **만나서 반갑습니다** (*mannaseo bangapseumnida*)."],
  ["how do you say see you later in korean | see you later in korean | korean for see you later", "In Korean, \"see you later\" is **이따 봐요** (*itta bwayo*). Also **나중에 봐요** (*najunge bwayo*). Casual: **이따 봐!**"],
  ["count to ten in korean | how do you count to 10 in korean | numbers 1 to 10 in korean", "Counting to ten in Korean:\n1 — **하나** (*hana*)\n2 — **둘** (*dul*)\n3 — **셋** (*set*)\n4 — **넷** (*net*)\n5 — **다섯** (*daseot*)\n6 — **여섯** (*yeoseot*)\n7 — **일곱** (*ilgop*)\n8 — **여덟** (*yeodeol*)\n9 — **아홉** (*ahop*)\n10 — **열** (*yeol*)\nKorean has a second set of numbers — **일 이 삼 사 오 육 칠 팔 구 십** (*il, i, sam, sa, o, yuk, chil, pal, gu, sip*) — used for money, dates and phone numbers."],
  ["days of the week in korean | how do you say monday in korean | korean days of the week", "The days of the week in Korean:\n• Monday — **월요일** (*woryoil*)\n• Tuesday — **화요일** (*hwayoil*)\n• Wednesday — **수요일** (*suyoil*)\n• Thursday — **목요일** (*mogyoil*)\n• Friday — **금요일** (*geumyoil*)\n• Saturday — **토요일** (*toyoil*)\n• Sunday — **일요일** (*iryoil*)\nLike Japanese, they're named after the moon, fire, water, wood, gold, earth and sun."],
  ["colors in korean | colours in korean | how do you say red in korean", "Colors in Korean:\n• Red — **빨간색** (*ppalgansaek*)\n• Orange — **주황색** (*juhwangsaek*)\n• Yellow — **노란색** (*noransaek*)\n• Green — **초록색** (*choroksaek*)\n• Blue — **파란색** (*paransaek*)\n• Purple — **보라색** (*borasaek*)\n• Black — **검은색** (*geomeunsaek*)\n• White — **흰색** (*huinsaek*)\n**색** (*saek*) means \"color\"."],
  ["how do you say good morning in thai | good morning in thai | thai for good morning", "In Thai, good morning is **สวัสดีตอนเช้า** (*sa-wat-dee ton CHAO*). Day to day, Thai people just say **สวัสดี** (*sa-wat-dee*) any time, adding **ครับ** (*khrap*) if you're a boy or man, or **ค่ะ** (*kha*) if you're a girl or woman."],
  ["how do you say good night in thai | good night in thai | goodnight in thai", "In Thai, good night is **ราตรีสวัสดิ์** (*raa-tree sa-WAT*). Among friends and family: **ฝันดี** (*fan dee*, sweet dreams)."],
  ["how do you say how are you in thai | how are you in thai | thai for how are you", "In Thai, \"how are you?\" is **สบายดีไหม** (*sa-baai dee MAI*). Reply: **สบายดี** (*sa-baai dee*, I'm fine). Add **ครับ/ค่ะ** to be polite."],
  ["how do you say my name is in thai | my name is in thai | what is your name in thai", "In Thai, \"my name is …\" is **ผมชื่อ …** (*phom CHUE*) — just add your name. That's for a boy or man; a girl or woman says **ฉันชื่อ …** (*chan CHUE*). To ask: **คุณชื่ออะไร** (*khun chue a-RAI*)"],
  ["how do you say i love you in thai | i love you in thai | thai for i love you", "In Thai, \"I love you\" is **ฉันรักคุณ** (*chan rak KHUN*). A boy or man often says **ผมรักคุณ** (*phom rak khun*). To family, kids say things like **รักแม่** (*rak MAE*, love you, Mom)."],
  ["how do you say happy birthday in thai | happy birthday in thai | thai for happy birthday", "In Thai, \"happy birthday\" is **สุขสันต์วันเกิด** (*suk-san wan GERT*)."],
  ["how do you say sorry in thai | how do you say excuse me in thai | sorry in thai | excuse me in thai", "In Thai, **ขอโทษ** (*khaw THOHT*) means both \"excuse me\" and \"sorry\". Add **ครับ** (*khrap*) or **ค่ะ** (*kha*) at the end to be polite."],
  ["how do you say where is the bathroom in thai | where is the bathroom in thai | where is the toilet in thai", "In Thai, \"where is the bathroom?\" is **ห้องน้ำอยู่ที่ไหน** (*hong NAAM yoo tee NAI*)."],
  ["how do you say i don't understand in thai | i don't understand in thai | i dont understand in thai", "In Thai, \"I don't understand\" is **ไม่เข้าใจ** (*mai khao JAI*)."],
  ["how do you say do you speak english in thai | do you speak english in thai | how to ask if someone speaks english in thai", "In Thai, \"do you speak English?\" is **พูดภาษาอังกฤษได้ไหม** (*phuut phaa-saa ang-GRIT dai MAI*)."],
  ["how do you say how much is this in thai | how much is this in thai | how much does it cost in thai", "In Thai, \"how much is this?\" is **อันนี้เท่าไหร่** (*an nee thao RAI*)."],
  ["how do you say nice to meet you in thai | nice to meet you in thai | thai for nice to meet you", "In Thai, \"nice to meet you\" is **ยินดีที่ได้รู้จัก** (*yin dee tee dai ROO-jak*)."],
  ["how do you say see you later in thai | see you later in thai | thai for see you later", "In Thai, \"see you later\" is **แล้วเจอกัน** (*laeo jer GAN*). Literally \"see each other then\"."],
  ["count to ten in thai | how do you count to 10 in thai | numbers 1 to 10 in thai", "Counting to ten in Thai:\n1 — **หนึ่ง** (*nueng*)\n2 — **สอง** (*song*)\n3 — **สาม** (*saam*)\n4 — **สี่** (*see*)\n5 — **ห้า** (*haa*)\n6 — **หก** (*hok*)\n7 — **เจ็ด** (*jet*)\n8 — **แปด** (*paet*)\n9 — **เก้า** (*gao*)\n10 — **สิบ** (*sip*)\nThai also has its own digits: ๑ ๒ ๓ ๔ ๕ ๖ ๗ ๘ ๙ ๑๐."],
  ["days of the week in thai | how do you say monday in thai | thai days of the week", "The days of the week in Thai:\n• Monday — **วันจันทร์** (*wan jan*)\n• Tuesday — **วันอังคาร** (*wan ang-khaan*)\n• Wednesday — **วันพุธ** (*wan phut*)\n• Thursday — **วันพฤหัสบดี** (*wan pha-rue-hat-sa-baw-dee*)\n• Friday — **วันศุกร์** (*wan suk*)\n• Saturday — **วันเสาร์** (*wan sao*)\n• Sunday — **วันอาทิตย์** (*wan aa-thit*)\nIn Thailand each day has its own color: Monday yellow, Tuesday pink, Wednesday green, Thursday orange, Friday blue, Saturday purple and Sunday red."],
  ["colors in thai | colours in thai | how do you say red in thai", "Colors in Thai:\n• Red — **สีแดง** (*sii daeng*)\n• Orange — **สีส้ม** (*sii som*)\n• Yellow — **สีเหลือง** (*sii lueang*)\n• Green — **สีเขียว** (*sii khiao*)\n• Blue — **สีน้ำเงิน** (*sii nam-ngoen*)\n• Purple — **สีม่วง** (*sii muang*)\n• Black — **สีดำ** (*sii dam*)\n• White — **สีขาว** (*sii khao*)\n**สี** (*sii*) means \"color\". Light sky blue has its own word: **สีฟ้า** (*sii faa*)."],
  ["which language has the most speakers | most widely spoken language | what language do the most people speak", "Counting everyone who speaks it (native speakers plus learners), **English** has the most speakers — about 1.5 billion. Counting only *native* speakers, **Mandarin Chinese** is number one with over 900 million, followed by **Spanish**."],
  ["easiest language to learn for english speakers | what is the easiest language to learn | easiest language for english speakers | which language is easiest to learn", "For English speakers, some of the easiest languages are **Spanish**, **Italian**, **Portuguese**, **French**, **Dutch**, **Norwegian** and **Swedish**. They use the same alphabet and share lots of words with English. Indonesian is also known for its simple grammar."],
  ["how many languages are spoken in the world | number of languages in the world | how many languages are there on earth", "There are about **7,000 languages** spoken in the world today! Around 40% of them are endangered, and just 23 languages are spoken by more than half of all people."],
  ["what languages do you know phrases in | which languages can you translate | what languages can you help with", "Even offline, I know handy phrases in 30 languages: Spanish, French, German, Italian, Portuguese, Dutch, Swedish, Norwegian, Danish, Finnish, Polish, Czech, Turkish, Vietnamese, Indonesian, Tagalog (Filipino), Swahili, Irish, Greek, Russian, Ukrainian, Arabic, Hebrew, Hindi, Bengali, Urdu, Mandarin Chinese, Japanese, Korean, Thai. Try asking things like *\"how do you say good morning in Japanese\"*, *\"count to ten in Swahili\"* or *\"colors in French\"*."],
  ["what is a tonal language | what does tonal language mean | which languages are tonal", "In a **tonal language**, the pitch of your voice changes a word's meaning. Mandarin has 4 main tones, Thai has 5 and Vietnamese has 6 — so *mā* (mom) and *mǎ* (horse) are different words in Mandarin!"],
  ["which languages are written right to left | right to left languages | what languages read from right to left", "**Arabic**, **Hebrew**, **Urdu** and **Persian (Farsi)** are written from right to left. Numbers, though, are usually still written left to right!"],
  ["what is pinyin | what does pinyin mean", "**Pinyin** is the official way to write Mandarin Chinese with Latin letters. For example, 你好 is written *nǐ hǎo*. The little marks show the tones."],
  ["what is romanization | what does romanization mean | what is romaji", "**Romanization** means writing a language in the Latin (A-B-C) alphabet so more people can read it — like *pinyin* for Chinese, *rōmaji* for Japanese or *ohayō* for おはよう. I add these in parentheses so you can say the phrases out loud."],
  ["what is a polyglot | what is someone who speaks many languages called | what do you call a person who speaks many languages", "A **polyglot** is someone who speaks several languages well. Someone who speaks two is **bilingual**, and three is **trilingual**."],
  ["what alphabet does russian use | what is the cyrillic alphabet | what is cyrillic", "**Cyrillic** is the alphabet used for Russian, Ukrainian, Bulgarian, Serbian and other languages. Russian Cyrillic has 33 letters — some look like Latin letters but sound different, like **Р** (r) and **Н** (n)!"],
  ["what are hiragana and katakana | what writing systems does japanese use | how many alphabets does japanese have", "Japanese mixes three writing systems: **hiragana** (ひらがな, for native words and grammar), **katakana** (カタカナ, for foreign words like オレンジ *orenji*) and **kanji** (漢字, characters borrowed from Chinese)."],
  ["what is hangul | what is the korean alphabet | who invented the korean alphabet", "**Hangul** (한글) is the Korean alphabet. It was created in 1443 under King Sejong the Great so everyone could learn to read. It has just 24 basic letters grouped into syllable blocks — like 한 (*han*)."]
);
